1
00:00:02,167 --> 00:00:04,937
(Morning of Day 3)

2
00:00:06,238 --> 00:00:09,908
(Do Gon and Ryun Gi eat breakfast.)

3
00:00:11,677 --> 00:00:13,412
(Satisfied)

4
00:00:14,746 --> 00:00:17,683
(Meanwhile, the women get ready.)

5
00:00:17,683 --> 00:00:20,085
Did everyone put theirs in the mailbox?

6
00:00:20,085 --> 00:00:21,787
I haven't put mine in yet.

7
00:00:21,787 --> 00:00:22,721
Me neither.

8
00:00:22,721 --> 00:00:23,689
What am I going to do?

9
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:28,794
(What must they put in the mailbox?)

10
00:00:29,061 --> 00:00:29,828
(Last night)

11
00:00:29,828 --> 00:00:31,163
I can't decide.

12
00:00:31,163 --> 00:00:32,297
I really don't know.

13
00:00:36,168 --> 00:00:39,371
(Jung Ye Ji, your bucket list date
with Kim Seon Ho is tomorrow.)

14
00:00:39,371 --> 00:00:42,241
(Please check the second-floor playroom.)

15
00:00:42,241 --> 00:00:43,075
(Startled)

16
00:00:44,076 --> 00:00:47,346
(She receives a mysterious text.)

17
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:53,285
(A secret text sent only to the women)

18
00:00:56,522 --> 00:00:58,323
(Focused)

19
00:01:00,893 --> 00:01:03,795
(Write down a bucket list activity
you want to do with your date.)

20
00:01:03,795 --> 00:01:06,565
(Put it in the mailbox tomorrow morning.)

21
00:01:06,565 --> 00:01:11,904
(A date to fulfill a long-held wish)

22
00:01:18,443 --> 00:01:21,580
(Write down an activity to do
with your matched date.)

23
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:24,683
(Secretly put it in the mailbox
tomorrow morning.)

24
00:01:25,651 --> 00:01:27,619
(Jung Yong Hwa)

25
00:01:27,619 --> 00:01:29,888
This is exciting.

26
00:01:29,888 --> 00:01:31,390
(Lee Se Young)

27
00:01:31,390 --> 00:01:34,193
They finally get to go on the date...

28
00:01:34,193 --> 00:01:37,029
they dreamed of while they were sick.

29
00:01:37,029 --> 00:01:38,597
- This is so exciting.
- This is great.

30
00:01:38,597 --> 00:01:39,798
I love this date idea.

31
00:01:39,798 --> 00:01:40,799
I can't wait.

32
00:01:40,799 --> 00:01:42,467
- This is the best.
- I love this date.

33
00:01:42,868 --> 00:01:44,169
(Agreed)

34
00:01:44,970 --> 00:01:50,442
(Jung Ye Ji and Kim Seon Ho)

35
00:01:50,943 --> 00:01:54,279
(Kim Na Young and Han Do Gon)

36
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:56,515
(Seo Ro Bin and Kim Jong Eun)

37
00:01:56,515 --> 00:01:58,150
(Seo Ro Bin and Han Do Gon)

38
00:01:58,650 --> 00:02:02,888
(Kang Min Young and Kim Seon Ho,
Kang Min Young and Kim Jong Eun)

39
00:02:03,755 --> 00:02:07,025
(Without the men knowing)

40
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:11,463
Only the women know their dates, right?

41
00:02:11,463 --> 00:02:14,066
- Right.
- The men have no idea.

42
00:02:14,066 --> 00:02:15,067
And on top of that,

43
00:02:15,067 --> 00:02:16,902
Ryun Gi and Do Gon were eating there.

44
00:02:16,902 --> 00:02:18,270
- They're guarding it.
- Right.

45
00:02:19,271 --> 00:02:21,073
I love rom-com.

46
00:02:21,073 --> 00:02:22,374
Me too.

47
00:02:22,708 --> 00:02:26,211
(Do Gon and Ryun Gi sit there unaware.)

48
00:02:26,545 --> 00:02:27,946
How did it get so late?

49
00:02:29,448 --> 00:02:31,650
(Na Young grabs her bucket list.)

50
00:02:32,284 --> 00:02:34,486
I'm in such a hurry right now.

51
00:02:34,486 --> 00:02:35,621
I can't think straight.

52
00:02:37,456 --> 00:02:39,958
(She composes herself and heads out.)

53
00:02:40,526 --> 00:02:41,460
(Glances)

54
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:46,164
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

55
00:02:47,065 --> 00:02:47,900
(Laughs)

56
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,902
(What was that?)

57
00:02:49,902 --> 00:02:51,169
At least she saw it.

58
00:02:51,169 --> 00:02:52,104
She's totally flustered.

59
00:02:52,104 --> 00:02:54,306
She obviously looks very suspicious.

60
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:56,875
At first, Na Young seemed like...

61
00:02:56,875 --> 00:02:58,810
She'd be the coldest one.

62
00:02:58,810 --> 00:03:00,312
But she's so cute when she's awkward.

63
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:02,414
Good morning.

64
00:03:02,414 --> 00:03:03,615
(An unexpected encounter with the men)

65
00:03:03,615 --> 00:03:05,050
Why are you eating there?

66
00:03:07,419 --> 00:03:08,153
What?

67
00:03:08,153 --> 00:03:08,820
Well...

68
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:09,555
What?

69
00:03:09,555 --> 00:03:11,089
I mean, nothing.

70
00:03:11,089 --> 00:03:12,157
Wait a second.

71
00:03:12,824 --> 00:03:14,059
(Scurries away)

72
00:03:19,698 --> 00:03:21,533
(Scurries away)

73
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:23,402
What am I supposed to do?

74
00:03:23,402 --> 00:03:26,038
We have to put it in the mailbox
on the wooden shelf, right?

75
00:03:26,038 --> 00:03:27,472
But they're eating right in front of it.

76
00:03:27,472 --> 00:03:28,540
- What?
- The men.

77
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:29,641
What?

78
00:03:29,641 --> 00:03:30,475
What?

79
00:03:30,475 --> 00:03:32,010
They're eating in the dining room.

80
00:03:32,010 --> 00:03:33,378
What do you mean?

81
00:03:33,579 --> 00:03:34,980
What's wrong, Na Young?

82
00:03:34,980 --> 00:03:36,849
They're eating in the dining room.

83
00:03:37,382 --> 00:03:38,350
The dining room...

84
00:03:38,350 --> 00:03:39,218
What?

85
00:03:40,686 --> 00:03:41,787
(The sudden news flusters the women.)

86
00:03:41,787 --> 00:03:42,855
Why did it have to be there?

87
00:03:43,755 --> 00:03:45,224
What do we do?

88
00:03:45,224 --> 00:03:46,358
I'm totally freaking out right now.

89
00:03:46,859 --> 00:03:47,826
Maybe...

90
00:03:48,427 --> 00:03:50,662
we could slip it in as we walk by.

91
00:03:52,431 --> 00:03:54,032
I need to wait for my chance.

92
00:03:55,601 --> 00:03:57,369
(Na Young makes another direct move.)

93
00:03:59,304 --> 00:04:00,539
(Sneaks over)

94
00:04:02,107 --> 00:04:03,709
- What are you doing?
- What?

95
00:04:03,709 --> 00:04:04,810
Why do you keep wandering around?

96
00:04:04,810 --> 00:04:06,011
No, that's not it.

97
00:04:06,011 --> 00:04:07,813
(Na Young is acting suspiciously.)

98
00:04:08,113 --> 00:04:09,147
I wanted to join you.

99
00:04:10,115 --> 00:04:11,517
We ate this by ourselves.

100
00:04:11,517 --> 00:04:12,384
It's okay.

101
00:04:12,384 --> 00:04:13,285
Should I clear the table for you?

102
00:04:13,285 --> 00:04:14,419
What are you talking about?

103
00:04:15,787 --> 00:04:19,224
(Rambling to avoid suspicion)

104
00:04:19,224 --> 00:04:20,025
Did you have breakfast?

105
00:04:20,025 --> 00:04:21,426
Your voice sounds a little hoarse.

106
00:04:21,426 --> 00:04:24,029
It's been like this.
This isn't my normal voice.

107
00:04:24,029 --> 00:04:25,030
It sounds worse.

108
00:04:25,030 --> 00:04:26,665
Make sure to drink something warm.

109
00:04:26,932 --> 00:04:28,233
(Turns away)

110
00:04:28,567 --> 00:04:30,369
(The mailbox remains just out of reach.)

111
00:04:30,369 --> 00:04:31,470
Definitely a movie.

112
00:04:31,470 --> 00:04:33,071
I really love watching movies too.

113
00:04:33,472 --> 00:04:35,707
(Forcing herself to react)

114
00:04:36,375 --> 00:04:39,978
(She puts the mission on hold.)

115
00:04:40,512 --> 00:04:42,981
(Ro Bin grows anxious.)

116
00:04:43,715 --> 00:04:45,584
(She hides her list in her hat,)

117
00:04:46,885 --> 00:04:48,520
(and hurries off.)

118
00:04:49,721 --> 00:04:51,490
(Scurries over)

119
00:04:54,793 --> 00:04:55,661
(Startled)

120
00:04:58,764 --> 00:04:59,965
No.

121
00:05:01,166 --> 00:05:02,401
(Startled)

122
00:05:02,401 --> 00:05:03,468
(They can't find out.)

123
00:05:03,468 --> 00:05:04,503
- No.
- What do we do?

124
00:05:05,204 --> 00:05:06,138
No.

125
00:05:06,672 --> 00:05:07,873
It fell where everyone could see it.

126
00:05:07,873 --> 00:05:09,041
No!

127
00:05:12,678 --> 00:05:15,147
(Ro Bin's bucket list goes flying.)

128
00:05:16,748 --> 00:05:19,451
(Everyone is watching Ro Bin.)

129
00:05:21,687 --> 00:05:22,654
(She throws herself to the floor.)

130
00:05:22,654 --> 00:05:23,789
Are you okay?

131
00:05:27,826 --> 00:05:28,827
She's cute.

132
00:05:28,827 --> 00:05:30,329
She literally dives for it.

133
00:05:30,329 --> 00:05:31,096
So cute.

134
00:05:31,997 --> 00:05:33,265
She's protecting her bucket list.

135
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:35,267
(Ro Bin puts her body on the line
to keep it top secret.)

136
00:05:35,267 --> 00:05:36,568
She's cute.

137
00:05:36,902 --> 00:05:38,837
It's funny how flustered she looks.

138
00:05:38,837 --> 00:05:39,705
Seriously.

139
00:05:41,106 --> 00:05:42,274
(Slowly lies down)

140
00:05:42,274 --> 00:05:43,509
Are you okay?

141
00:05:44,076 --> 00:05:45,878
(Na Young backs her up.)

142
00:05:45,878 --> 00:05:47,513
- What?
- Are you sure you're okay?

143
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:49,715
That didn't look like you tripped.

144
00:05:49,715 --> 00:05:51,049
No.

145
00:05:51,049 --> 00:05:52,317
Come here.

146
00:05:52,317 --> 00:05:53,852
That was slapstick, right?

147
00:05:53,852 --> 00:05:56,321
- You wanted to make us laugh here.
- Yes, that's right.

148
00:05:56,321 --> 00:05:57,489
It was really funny.

149
00:05:58,957 --> 00:06:01,360
- Why are you here, though?
- Exactly.

150
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:02,895
(Flustered)

151
00:06:03,328 --> 00:06:05,531
(The bucket list clutched to her chest)

152
00:06:05,931 --> 00:06:08,166
(Stares)

153
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:10,002
They close one at a time?

154
00:06:10,002 --> 00:06:11,870
Right. I just realized that.

155
00:06:12,938 --> 00:06:15,307
(Day 2)

156
00:06:15,307 --> 00:06:16,542
I just realized it.

157
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:17,943
What did you say?

158
00:06:17,943 --> 00:06:21,680
It says Day 1 and Day 2.

159
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:25,717
(Ro Bin helps crack the mailbox system.)

160
00:06:26,118 --> 00:06:27,486
What is this?

161
00:06:27,486 --> 00:06:28,554
I know. What is that?

162
00:06:28,921 --> 00:06:30,956
It's so pretty. It's made of wood.

163
00:06:32,457 --> 00:06:33,592
(Reading the room)

164
00:06:36,662 --> 00:06:37,696
What's going on?

165
00:06:39,531 --> 00:06:42,467
(Min Young casually joins them.)

166
00:06:42,467 --> 00:06:44,403
Sorry. We ate toast without you.

167
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:45,704
But why do you...

168
00:06:45,704 --> 00:06:47,973
- never ask us to join?
- What?

169
00:06:47,973 --> 00:06:50,843
Why don't you ask us to have breakfast?

170
00:06:50,843 --> 00:06:53,412
I don't know when you wake up.

171
00:06:53,412 --> 00:06:55,347
Why don't you ask us to have breakfast?

172
00:06:56,415 --> 00:06:58,450
(Na Young escapes in the meantime.)

173
00:06:58,450 --> 00:06:59,918
We did the same thing yesterday.

174
00:06:59,918 --> 00:07:02,387
The second floor is a private space.

175
00:07:02,387 --> 00:07:04,556
If we go up first and talk there...

176
00:07:04,556 --> 00:07:05,691
Then I'll do this.

177
00:07:06,992 --> 00:07:10,762
(Operation, Scold and Distract)

178
00:07:11,163 --> 00:07:13,632
(She'll sneak it in while they're busy.)

179
00:07:15,267 --> 00:07:16,068
(Attempt)

180
00:07:16,068 --> 00:07:18,170
You always talk among yourselves.

181
00:07:18,170 --> 00:07:19,771
We tell you to come out before we talk.

182
00:07:19,771 --> 00:07:21,940
That's what I don't like. I don't like it.

183
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:24,176
Why wait until someone invites you down?

184
00:07:24,176 --> 00:07:25,344
Let's all hang out.

185
00:07:25,344 --> 00:07:27,079
We keep glancing over at you, right?

186
00:07:27,079 --> 00:07:30,115
That's our way of asking you
to ask us to join you.

187
00:07:30,115 --> 00:07:31,783
You should come over yourselves.

188
00:07:33,886 --> 00:07:35,020
Hurry up and do the dishes.

189
00:07:36,355 --> 00:07:37,589
Now she's suddenly ordering us around.

190
00:07:37,589 --> 00:07:39,758
Just hurry up and finish the dishes.

191
00:07:39,758 --> 00:07:41,560
Then we can all have some tea.

192
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:43,996
Okay. Let's have tea.

193
00:07:43,996 --> 00:07:45,831
(All over the place)

194
00:07:45,831 --> 00:07:47,599
Why do you keep wandering around?

195
00:07:49,334 --> 00:07:51,837
(A clearly suspicious walk)

196
00:07:51,837 --> 00:07:53,939
They're like a whole cast of characters.

197
00:07:53,939 --> 00:07:55,607
They all have such distinct personalities.

198
00:07:56,441 --> 00:07:57,442
If those two are done,

199
00:07:57,442 --> 00:07:59,111
they should get moving.

200
00:07:59,978 --> 00:08:01,113
I wish they'd hurry up and leave.

201
00:08:01,113 --> 00:08:02,748
How can they be so oblivious?

202
00:08:02,748 --> 00:08:04,850
- This is driving me crazy.
- What are they doing?

203
00:08:05,651 --> 00:08:06,885
I'm the one losing my mind.

204
00:08:06,885 --> 00:08:09,154
Ryun Gi, Do Gon, just go inside now.

205
00:08:11,023 --> 00:08:12,791
(Stands up)

206
00:08:12,791 --> 00:08:13,825
Should we clear the table?

207
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:18,130
(The two men finally leave
the dining room.)

208
00:08:18,463 --> 00:08:19,831
(Sneaks over)

209
00:08:21,033 --> 00:08:24,469
(She finally gets her list in.)

210
00:08:25,504 --> 00:08:26,972
(Slips it in)

211
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:30,475
(Na Young, after all the detours)

212
00:08:30,475 --> 00:08:34,012
(And finally, Ye Ji)

213
00:08:35,314 --> 00:08:38,483
(All the women's lists make it safely in.)

214
00:08:38,483 --> 00:08:40,485
(To Seon Ho)

215
00:08:40,485 --> 00:08:43,388
(Jong Eun)

216
00:08:43,388 --> 00:08:46,725
(To Do Gon)

217
00:08:47,359 --> 00:08:50,596
(Do Gon gets ready to go out.)

218
00:08:56,869 --> 00:09:00,305
(Han Do Gon, your date has been matched.)

219
00:09:00,305 --> 00:09:02,674
(Check the mailbox before you leave.)

220
00:09:04,142 --> 00:09:09,915
(The women's lists arrive for the men.)

221
00:09:13,218 --> 00:09:17,756
(From Na Young, From Ro Bin)

222
00:09:19,992 --> 00:09:25,564
(From Min Young, From Ye Ji)

223
00:09:27,065 --> 00:09:32,905
(From Ro Bin, From Min Young)

224
00:09:36,408 --> 00:09:40,879
(Can they have their dream dates today?)

225
00:09:55,227 --> 00:09:56,628
(Grins)

226
00:09:57,796 --> 00:09:58,830
Hello.

227
00:09:58,830 --> 00:10:01,066
(Ro Bin and Jong Eun's first date begins.)

228
00:10:01,567 --> 00:10:03,101
Just seeing him there...

229
00:10:03,101 --> 00:10:04,536
made my heart flutter.

230
00:10:06,071 --> 00:10:08,740
By giving him all of my time,

231
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:12,311
I got to be with the person
I'd wanted to be with.

232
00:10:14,546 --> 00:10:15,447
Here it is.

233
00:10:15,447 --> 00:10:17,583
(Ro Bin takes Jong Eun somewhere.)

234
00:10:17,583 --> 00:10:18,784
Do you know where we're going?

235
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:19,618
Table tennis.

236
00:10:20,886 --> 00:10:21,587
That's right.

237
00:10:21,587 --> 00:10:23,388
You like playing table tennis, right?

238
00:10:23,388 --> 00:10:24,456
I do.

239
00:10:25,090 --> 00:10:25,924
This is it.

240
00:10:29,494 --> 00:10:31,563
Playing table tennis together.

241
00:10:32,598 --> 00:10:35,634
I was on the team in elementary school...

242
00:10:35,634 --> 00:10:37,870
and played until middle school.

243
00:10:37,870 --> 00:10:40,105
If I had a boyfriend,
we'd go to play table tennis.

244
00:10:40,105 --> 00:10:43,342
I'm good, so I could impress him.

245
00:10:43,342 --> 00:10:44,243
I can do it.

246
00:10:45,911 --> 00:10:49,314
Do you make bets when you play?

247
00:10:49,314 --> 00:10:50,949
Do you want to make a bet?

248
00:10:50,949 --> 00:10:52,684
- Sure.
- I'd love to.

249
00:10:55,521 --> 00:10:58,724
(Will today's date bring them closer?)

250
00:10:59,124 --> 00:11:01,193
I'm taking this off. It's hot.

251
00:11:01,193 --> 00:11:01,994
Are you hot?

252
00:11:01,994 --> 00:11:03,128
(They decide to bet on the match.)

253
00:11:03,495 --> 00:11:04,997
What should we bet on?

254
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:05,864
What should we bet on?

255
00:11:06,965 --> 00:11:08,000
What should we bet on?

256
00:11:10,602 --> 00:11:11,570
What do you want?

257
00:11:12,070 --> 00:11:12,905
Maybe...

258
00:11:13,438 --> 00:11:14,439
a wish?

259
00:11:14,973 --> 00:11:16,542
- Granting a wish?
- Granting a wish?

260
00:11:17,743 --> 00:11:18,610
The loser does it?

261
00:11:19,077 --> 00:11:20,112
(A match with a wish on the line.)

262
00:11:20,112 --> 00:11:21,046
Okay.

263
00:11:21,046 --> 00:11:22,281
Okay.

264
00:11:22,281 --> 00:11:23,582
I'm nervous again.

265
00:11:24,416 --> 00:11:26,618
I'm nervous because I'll play seriously.

266
00:11:26,618 --> 00:11:27,653
You should.

267
00:11:28,687 --> 00:11:29,588
But...

268
00:11:30,522 --> 00:11:33,559
we shouldn't go easy on each other, right?

269
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:34,860
- Right.
- Right?

270
00:11:35,427 --> 00:11:36,628
For real?

271
00:11:37,095 --> 00:11:37,930
For real?

272
00:11:37,930 --> 00:11:38,730
We're really going all out.

273
00:11:39,932 --> 00:11:41,266
Is this really a good idea?

274
00:11:42,201 --> 00:11:43,001
Okay.

275
00:11:43,535 --> 00:11:45,370
- Am I serving?
- Yes.

276
00:11:46,738 --> 00:11:50,142
(Nervous)

277
00:11:50,976 --> 00:11:52,277
(Laughs)

278
00:11:58,150 --> 00:11:59,318
- One to zero.
- One to zero.

279
00:11:59,318 --> 00:12:00,185
(Ro Bin drops the first point.)

280
00:12:03,088 --> 00:12:03,789
(Smash)

281
00:12:05,557 --> 00:12:06,458
Seriously?

282
00:12:06,458 --> 00:12:08,694
Now you're throwing in smashes.

283
00:12:10,329 --> 00:12:11,830
(Glares)

284
00:12:12,130 --> 00:12:13,098
Look at her eyes.

285
00:12:14,066 --> 00:12:16,235
(Ro Bin's eyes blaze with determination.)

286
00:12:16,235 --> 00:12:18,103
- Ro Bin came to win.
- Whatever it takes.

287
00:12:19,238 --> 00:12:21,540
I can't tell how badly she wants to win.

288
00:12:22,808 --> 00:12:23,675
She really wants to win.

289
00:12:23,675 --> 00:12:25,043
Her eyes weren't smiling.

290
00:12:26,178 --> 00:12:27,145
Only her lips were.

291
00:12:28,413 --> 00:12:29,715
- One to one.
- One to one.

292
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:34,553
(An intense match for a first date)

293
00:12:35,187 --> 00:12:37,456
(Kim Jong Eun's impenetrable defense)

294
00:12:37,456 --> 00:12:39,691
(Seo Ro Bin, master of the smash)

295
00:12:41,193 --> 00:12:43,295
You've been hiding your skills.

296
00:12:44,363 --> 00:12:45,597
I need to win.

297
00:12:45,597 --> 00:12:46,365
Two to two.

298
00:12:46,365 --> 00:12:49,401
My competitive streak kept kicking in.

299
00:12:49,401 --> 00:12:52,538
She was so good, it caught me off guard.

300
00:12:54,006 --> 00:12:56,775
(They both give it their all.)

301
00:12:58,977 --> 00:13:02,114
(Who will get their wish granted?)

302
00:13:04,917 --> 00:13:07,519
(Jong Eun wins.)

303
00:13:08,987 --> 00:13:10,789
You're really good, though.

304
00:13:10,789 --> 00:13:11,990
I lost.

305
00:13:11,990 --> 00:13:13,158
That's too bad.

306
00:13:13,525 --> 00:13:14,426
I'm good, right?

307
00:13:14,893 --> 00:13:16,195
You're so good.

308
00:13:16,195 --> 00:13:17,462
I got the hang of it at the end.

309
00:13:19,531 --> 00:13:20,899
In the end,

310
00:13:20,899 --> 00:13:22,534
I lost.

311
00:13:22,534 --> 00:13:23,502
I lost,

312
00:13:24,870 --> 00:13:25,804
but I wanted to lose.

313
00:13:25,804 --> 00:13:27,539
I was so happy I lost.

314
00:13:28,073 --> 00:13:29,875
I was so curious.

315
00:13:29,875 --> 00:13:32,678
The loser had to grant the winner a wish.

316
00:13:32,678 --> 00:13:33,879
I couldn't wait to hear...

317
00:13:33,879 --> 00:13:36,849
what Jong Eun would ask of me.

318
00:13:36,849 --> 00:13:39,918
(Jong Eun beats her competitive streak
and leaves her wanting to know more.)

319
00:13:40,285 --> 00:13:41,553
Sit here.

320
00:13:41,553 --> 00:13:42,354
Okay.

321
00:13:43,989 --> 00:13:45,524
I'm curious about something.

322
00:13:45,524 --> 00:13:49,127
How did you feel
when I gave you that note?

323
00:13:49,127 --> 00:13:50,662
I was really surprised.

324
00:13:50,662 --> 00:13:51,897
- Surprised?
- Yes.

325
00:13:51,897 --> 00:13:53,332
Were you really surprised?

326
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:55,434
You didn't expect it at all?

327
00:13:55,434 --> 00:13:58,370
While I've been in the house,

328
00:13:59,438 --> 00:14:01,006
the people I've talked to most...

329
00:14:01,607 --> 00:14:04,743
were Min Young and Na Young.

330
00:14:04,743 --> 00:14:06,411
- Min Young and Na Young?
- Yes.

331
00:14:07,479 --> 00:14:08,714
So...

332
00:14:08,714 --> 00:14:09,414
I never...

333
00:14:09,414 --> 00:14:11,049
You never expected it, and that's all?

334
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:13,051
(Flustered)

335
00:14:13,051 --> 00:14:15,320
I'm not criticizing you.
I'm just asking if that was all.

336
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:16,455
- So...
- Yes.

337
00:14:17,990 --> 00:14:20,292
I mean, we'd only...

338
00:14:20,292 --> 00:14:22,728
spoken a few times in passing.

339
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:25,531
I just thought...

340
00:14:26,298 --> 00:14:28,200
you were making conversation...

341
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:30,903
whenever you spoke to me.

342
00:14:30,903 --> 00:14:32,171
I see.

343
00:14:32,171 --> 00:14:33,739
I honestly had no idea.

344
00:14:33,739 --> 00:14:36,141
Didn't you want to talk to me?

345
00:14:36,141 --> 00:14:37,743
It'd be nice to talk.

346
00:14:37,743 --> 00:14:38,710
No, I mean,

347
00:14:39,144 --> 00:14:41,313
did you actually want to talk to me?

348
00:14:41,313 --> 00:14:42,314
Well,

349
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:44,917
I wanted to get to know...

350
00:14:44,917 --> 00:14:46,351
everyone one at a time.

351
00:14:46,351 --> 00:14:47,819
Did you want to talk to me?

352
00:14:47,819 --> 00:14:48,854
Yes.

353
00:14:51,990 --> 00:14:55,127
(Their conversation hits a glitch.)

354
00:14:55,127 --> 00:14:57,729
Why are these two so funny?

355
00:14:57,729 --> 00:15:00,465
Give him a prompt, and the AI responds.

356
00:15:00,465 --> 00:15:01,867
He only gives you the output.

357
00:15:01,867 --> 00:15:03,435
- So that's what it was?
- That's it.

358
00:15:03,435 --> 00:15:04,369
AI Jong Eun.

359
00:15:04,369 --> 00:15:06,338
He answers whatever you ask.

360
00:15:06,338 --> 00:15:07,339
"What did you do?"

361
00:15:07,339 --> 00:15:08,140
"I did that."

362
00:15:08,140 --> 00:15:09,575
"I shouldn't let you win, right?"

363
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:10,709
"Right. We should play hard."

364
00:15:10,709 --> 00:15:11,677
(He sticks strictly to the prompt.)

365
00:15:11,677 --> 00:15:12,511
This is driving me crazy.

366
00:15:12,511 --> 00:15:15,147
Did he really come
just to play table tennis?

367
00:15:15,147 --> 00:15:16,448
That's just how Jong Eun is.

368
00:15:17,749 --> 00:15:18,984
(Riveted)

369
00:15:21,386 --> 00:15:22,554
(Glances)

370
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:25,591
- You're checking the time.
- No, it's not that.

371
00:15:26,058 --> 00:15:27,326
Why? Are you getting bored?

372
00:15:27,526 --> 00:15:28,961
- No, it's just...
- Are you okay?

373
00:15:29,995 --> 00:15:32,331
It's time for me to take my medicine.

374
00:15:32,331 --> 00:15:33,165
You can take it.

375
00:15:33,765 --> 00:15:35,467
- Hold on.
- Sure.

376
00:15:40,639 --> 00:15:42,608
Do you want this too, Ro Bin?

377
00:15:42,608 --> 00:15:43,542
What is it?

378
00:15:43,542 --> 00:15:44,676
Is that a banana?

379
00:15:44,676 --> 00:15:46,111
Yes. I like bananas.

380
00:15:46,111 --> 00:15:48,013
But have you eaten anything?

381
00:15:48,013 --> 00:15:50,382
- No, not a thing.
- Really?

382
00:15:50,382 --> 00:15:52,951
Then you should drink this
before the banana.

383
00:15:52,951 --> 00:15:54,653
Bananas aren't good on an empty stomach.

384
00:15:54,653 --> 00:15:55,354
Really?

385
00:15:55,354 --> 00:15:57,589
They say bananas are best after a meal.

386
00:15:57,589 --> 00:15:58,624
Have this first.

387
00:15:58,624 --> 00:15:59,925
There's a fixed time to take my medicine.

388
00:15:59,925 --> 00:16:01,593
- I see.
- Yes.

389
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:04,363
And I can't take it on an empty stomach.

390
00:16:04,363 --> 00:16:05,297
It's a hassle, isn't it?

391
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:08,233
Not at all. I've been through it too.

392
00:16:09,468 --> 00:16:12,538
I had a bone marrow transplant too,
so I know.

393
00:16:13,672 --> 00:16:14,773
I totally get it.

394
00:16:24,049 --> 00:16:27,920
I thought you were so quiet, Jong Eun.

395
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,454
Me?

396
00:16:29,454 --> 00:16:32,624
You chime in when we're all together,

397
00:16:32,624 --> 00:16:34,493
but when you're one-on-one,

398
00:16:34,493 --> 00:16:36,795
I haven't heard you say much.

399
00:16:36,795 --> 00:16:38,096
One-on-one?

400
00:16:38,964 --> 00:16:39,831
Kind of...

401
00:16:40,899 --> 00:16:42,668
I'm not sure. That's just how I am.

402
00:16:43,135 --> 00:16:45,037
Are you really shy around new people?

403
00:16:45,037 --> 00:16:47,339
I've always been super shy.

404
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:49,274
I was just curious.

405
00:16:49,875 --> 00:16:52,311
We haven't talked much,

406
00:16:52,311 --> 00:16:54,313
so I really wondered what you're like.

407
00:16:54,313 --> 00:16:55,714
Ro Bin,

408
00:16:55,714 --> 00:16:58,050
do you make the first move...

409
00:16:58,050 --> 00:17:00,118
or do you wait for them?

410
00:17:00,118 --> 00:17:02,154
I think I usually make the first move.

411
00:17:02,154 --> 00:17:03,622
How do you do that?

412
00:17:04,156 --> 00:17:05,557
How do I do it?

413
00:17:05,557 --> 00:17:06,525
I mean,

414
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:08,160
how do you show them you like them?

415
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:10,696
How do I show it?

416
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:12,965
Well, I...

417
00:17:14,366 --> 00:17:16,568
She's doing it right now.

418
00:17:16,568 --> 00:17:17,970
Like that.

419
00:17:17,970 --> 00:17:20,239
- She's talking to you now.
- She is, Jong Eun.

420
00:17:20,239 --> 00:17:21,740
- She keeps asking questions.
- Jong Eun.

421
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:23,041
Jong Eun is killing me.

422
00:17:25,944 --> 00:17:28,947
(Everyone squirms along with Ro Bin.)

423
00:17:29,815 --> 00:17:32,651
I guess I just keep trying to talk.

424
00:17:32,651 --> 00:17:34,853
You say something as you pass by?
Really?

425
00:17:34,853 --> 00:17:37,022
Yes, I try to start a conversation.

426
00:17:37,456 --> 00:17:38,957
(Nods)

427
00:17:38,957 --> 00:17:39,791
I guess so.

428
00:17:39,791 --> 00:17:42,528
(In fact, Ro Bin...)

429
00:17:42,528 --> 00:17:44,196
(Evening of Day 2)

430
00:17:44,196 --> 00:17:45,497
Wait, what happened to your hand?

431
00:17:45,998 --> 00:17:47,065
Earlier, I just...

432
00:17:47,065 --> 00:17:48,033
What happened? Are you hurt?

433
00:17:48,033 --> 00:17:49,268
No, I'm fine.

434
00:17:52,137 --> 00:17:54,339
Didn't you cut it pretty deep?

435
00:17:54,339 --> 00:17:56,475
I'm fine. It's nothing serious.

436
00:17:56,475 --> 00:17:58,310
But it could get infected.

437
00:17:58,310 --> 00:18:02,014
So I disinfected it and bandaged it.

438
00:18:02,014 --> 00:18:03,315
Good. That's a relief.

439
00:18:03,315 --> 00:18:04,683
(She couldn't stop thinking
about his cut.)

440
00:18:07,486 --> 00:18:09,755
- Sore throat medicine.
- Here it is.

441
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:10,756
Sore throat medicine.

442
00:18:11,290 --> 00:18:12,758
(Glances)

443
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:16,595
That cut looks pretty bad.

444
00:18:16,595 --> 00:18:19,031
It bled a lot.

445
00:18:19,031 --> 00:18:21,133
You really need to be careful.

446
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:23,569
Did you bandage it?

447
00:18:23,569 --> 00:18:24,436
Yes.

448
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:26,805
(She starts a conversation with Jong Eun.)

449
00:18:26,805 --> 00:18:28,340
- You're taking your medicine now, right?
- Yes.

450
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:29,608
Do you want me to do it for you now?

451
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:30,409
Do what?

452
00:18:30,409 --> 00:18:31,743
- This.
- Yes.

453
00:18:34,046 --> 00:18:35,647
(Gently)

454
00:18:36,849 --> 00:18:39,618
I hadn't exactly...

455
00:18:40,185 --> 00:18:41,920
told Jong Eun directly how I felt.

456
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:43,589
So of course he might not have noticed.

457
00:18:43,589 --> 00:18:45,624
But I thought I'd shown him...

458
00:18:45,624 --> 00:18:47,526
little signs here and there.

459
00:18:47,526 --> 00:18:50,295
But I can see how he could've missed them.

460
00:18:51,196 --> 00:18:53,599
(Last night in the Room of Time)

461
00:18:56,368 --> 00:19:01,773
(100 minutes filled with
feelings she'd built up over time)

462
00:19:02,207 --> 00:19:02,941
(Touched)

463
00:19:02,941 --> 00:19:04,209
Look at that.

464
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:06,211
Ro Bin really has...

465
00:19:06,211 --> 00:19:07,346
had eyes only for him.

466
00:19:07,346 --> 00:19:09,648
She's completely devoted.

467
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:11,517
Then this must be...

468
00:19:11,517 --> 00:19:12,885
so hard for Ro Bin.

469
00:19:12,885 --> 00:19:14,219
What is she supposed to do?

470
00:19:14,219 --> 00:19:16,154
She thinks she's been showing him.

471
00:19:16,154 --> 00:19:16,955
Exactly.

472
00:19:16,955 --> 00:19:19,258
But he doesn't get it.

473
00:19:19,258 --> 00:19:20,726
What is love?

474
00:19:20,726 --> 00:19:21,894
"What is love?"

475
00:19:21,894 --> 00:19:24,229
- Seriously, what is love?
- What is it?

476
00:19:24,229 --> 00:19:25,230
Right.

477
00:19:25,230 --> 00:19:27,466
(Will Ro Bin's feelings reach Jong Eun?)

478
00:19:27,733 --> 00:19:29,401
Is there anything you want to ask me?

479
00:19:31,570 --> 00:19:33,005
Something I want to ask?

480
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:34,506
Can I ask you later?

481
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:36,008
So you do have a question?

482
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:37,476
Maybe I'll ask over a meal.

483
00:19:38,477 --> 00:19:40,479
Maybe I do.

484
00:19:46,652 --> 00:19:47,553
(They head to Ro Bin's chosen restaurant.)

485
00:19:47,553 --> 00:19:48,754
You're always cheerful.

486
00:19:48,754 --> 00:19:49,521
Me?

487
00:19:50,322 --> 00:19:51,723
I like that you always seem so upbeat.

488
00:19:51,723 --> 00:19:53,091
Really? Thank you.

489
00:19:54,159 --> 00:19:55,394
You know where we're going, right?

490
00:19:55,394 --> 00:19:56,228
Yes. I'll...

491
00:19:56,228 --> 00:19:57,462
lead the way.

492
00:19:57,462 --> 00:19:58,430
Nice.

493
00:19:58,931 --> 00:19:59,798
You're taking the lead?

494
00:20:01,633 --> 00:20:02,901
Does this count?

495
00:20:04,770 --> 00:20:06,471
There. That's it.

496
00:20:06,471 --> 00:20:08,273
- This place? Go on in.
- Okay.

497
00:20:15,013 --> 00:20:19,151
(They arrive during the break.)

498
00:20:19,418 --> 00:20:20,319
Aren't you cold?

499
00:20:20,319 --> 00:20:21,186
No, I'm not cold.

500
00:20:21,186 --> 00:20:23,589
You look colder in just a T-shirt
beneath that.

501
00:20:24,356 --> 00:20:25,757
Your sweater is full of holes.

502
00:20:25,757 --> 00:20:26,658
I'm fine.

503
00:20:26,658 --> 00:20:28,126
It's knit. I'm fine.

504
00:20:28,126 --> 00:20:29,461
The wind must cut right through it.

505
00:20:29,461 --> 00:20:32,164
It's freezing, and you're taking it off?

506
00:20:32,164 --> 00:20:33,565
- I'm not very cold.
- You're not?

507
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,368
Are you letting me wear it?

508
00:20:37,169 --> 00:20:38,070
Thank you.

509
00:20:38,503 --> 00:20:39,805
It may be big on you.

510
00:20:39,805 --> 00:20:41,006
Of course, it will be.

511
00:20:41,006 --> 00:20:42,875
(Jong Eun gives Ro Bin his jacket.)

512
00:20:42,875 --> 00:20:44,309
- I'm much smaller than you.
- Is it okay?

513
00:20:44,309 --> 00:20:46,278
I'm fine. It isn't heavy.

514
00:20:47,279 --> 00:20:48,347
What?

515
00:20:48,347 --> 00:20:49,848
Don't do that if you don't like her.

516
00:20:49,848 --> 00:20:51,517
That would make my heart race.

517
00:20:51,517 --> 00:20:53,151
Right. Because you'd feel his warmth...

518
00:20:54,052 --> 00:20:57,456
and even smell his cologne on it.

519
00:20:57,456 --> 00:20:58,624
Exactly.

520
00:20:58,624 --> 00:21:00,325
You're wrapped up in something he wore...

521
00:21:00,325 --> 00:21:01,226
and it's keeping you warm?

522
00:21:01,226 --> 00:21:02,294
(Snickers)

523
00:21:03,028 --> 00:21:05,097
Have you done that before?

524
00:21:05,097 --> 00:21:06,465
(Flustered)

525
00:21:06,999 --> 00:21:07,966
Give me your jacket.

526
00:21:07,966 --> 00:21:08,800
(Laughs)

527
00:21:09,835 --> 00:21:11,036
Give me your jacket.

528
00:21:11,036 --> 00:21:12,971
(That was oddly specific.)

529
00:21:12,971 --> 00:21:14,940
I just want to see how it feels.

530
00:21:15,474 --> 00:21:16,842
That's hilarious.

531
00:21:19,344 --> 00:21:20,345
It isn't heavy.

532
00:21:20,345 --> 00:21:22,080
But you're only wearing a T-shirt.

533
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:23,315
Me? It's nice and cool.

534
00:21:23,315 --> 00:21:24,183
You're not cold?

535
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:26,985
What is ochazuke?

536
00:21:26,985 --> 00:21:27,786
It's kind of...

537
00:21:27,786 --> 00:21:29,121
A traditional Japanese dish?

538
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:33,659
It's mild and not heavily seasoned.

539
00:21:33,659 --> 00:21:36,161
Do you like milder food too?

540
00:21:36,762 --> 00:21:38,330
Food that's not heavily seasoned?

541
00:21:38,330 --> 00:21:39,765
Yes. I like everything.

542
00:21:40,232 --> 00:21:43,402
Jong Eun gave me his jacket.

543
00:21:43,402 --> 00:21:44,903
That gesture...

544
00:21:45,571 --> 00:21:46,538
made my heart race.

545
00:21:46,538 --> 00:21:49,908
I felt warm the second I put it on.

546
00:21:49,908 --> 00:21:54,279
Jong Eun once told me...

547
00:21:54,279 --> 00:21:58,116
he expresses himself more through actions.

548
00:21:58,116 --> 00:21:59,551
So...

549
00:21:59,551 --> 00:22:02,120
was that his way of showing he cared?

550
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:03,722
I couldn't help wondering.

551
00:22:05,224 --> 00:22:06,758
Maybe I'm just reading into it.

552
00:22:09,294 --> 00:22:11,063
(A moment she wants to read as interest)

553
00:22:11,063 --> 00:22:14,299
They said eel isn't available today.

554
00:22:14,299 --> 00:22:15,267
Really?

555
00:22:20,806 --> 00:22:23,308
(Meanwhile)

556
00:22:27,813 --> 00:22:29,515
Are you ready?

557
00:22:30,482 --> 00:22:31,517
You startled me.

558
00:22:33,552 --> 00:22:35,654
(Min Young changes into a school uniform.)

559
00:22:35,654 --> 00:22:36,555
Ready to go?

560
00:22:36,555 --> 00:22:37,523
That looks great on you.

561
00:22:37,523 --> 00:22:39,424
Really? Do I pass for a student?

562
00:22:39,424 --> 00:22:40,292
You really do.

563
00:22:40,993 --> 00:22:42,127
- My goodness.
- So cute.

564
00:22:42,127 --> 00:22:44,429
She's so cute.

565
00:22:44,796 --> 00:22:46,431
She looks like a student.

566
00:22:46,431 --> 00:22:47,599
It really suits her.

567
00:22:47,599 --> 00:22:49,067
It does. She looks great.

568
00:22:49,067 --> 00:22:51,270
I can't wait to see this date.

569
00:22:51,270 --> 00:22:52,704
A school uniform date.

570
00:22:54,473 --> 00:22:58,310
(Kang Min Young's bucket list,
a date in school uniforms)

571
00:22:58,310 --> 00:23:01,413
My friends always went for
spicy rice cakes in middle school.

572
00:23:01,413 --> 00:23:03,182
I was so jealous every time.

573
00:23:03,182 --> 00:23:04,283
Back then,

574
00:23:04,283 --> 00:23:05,884
my leg was in bad shape,

575
00:23:05,884 --> 00:23:07,686
so I couldn't go out for spicy rice cakes.

576
00:23:07,686 --> 00:23:10,122
I always went straight home.

577
00:23:10,122 --> 00:23:14,026
I wanted to wear a uniform,

578
00:23:14,026 --> 00:23:16,461
eat spicy rice cakes,
and make that memory.

579
00:23:18,030 --> 00:23:20,532
Hearing that made me want to try my best.

580
00:23:20,532 --> 00:23:23,902
I wanted to make it unforgettable for her.

581
00:23:24,836 --> 00:23:29,074
(Min Young and Seon Ho's camcorder date)

582
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:33,545
- You chose the right pants.
- What?

583
00:23:33,545 --> 00:23:34,947
They look like a good fit.

584
00:23:34,947 --> 00:23:36,014
Really? That's a relief.

585
00:23:36,014 --> 00:23:36,882
Shall we go?

586
00:23:37,416 --> 00:23:38,483
Let's go.

587
00:23:38,483 --> 00:23:39,484
(Back in their school days)

588
00:23:45,157 --> 00:23:47,860
Let's film whenever we see a good shot.

589
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:49,194
Tell me, and I'll get it.

590
00:23:49,194 --> 00:23:50,662
No, that's not the point.

591
00:23:50,662 --> 00:23:52,664
- I just do it?
- We both just film.

592
00:23:52,664 --> 00:23:53,999
I'll film whenever I want.

593
00:23:53,999 --> 00:23:56,501
Asking first would make it look staged.

594
00:23:56,501 --> 00:23:58,503
But I'm left-handed,

595
00:23:58,503 --> 00:23:59,738
so the camera might shake a little.

596
00:23:59,738 --> 00:24:00,839
- Really?
- Yes.

597
00:24:00,839 --> 00:24:03,809
I had no idea...

598
00:24:03,809 --> 00:24:06,712
you'd go on a date with me.

599
00:24:06,712 --> 00:24:09,815
We haven't had a chance to talk,
not even at the House.

600
00:24:09,815 --> 00:24:12,384
It's still awkward to ask to talk alone.

601
00:24:12,384 --> 00:24:13,619
So I thought...

602
00:24:13,619 --> 00:24:18,056
a date was the only way we'd get to talk.

603
00:24:18,056 --> 00:24:19,691
I was really surprised.

604
00:24:19,691 --> 00:24:22,528
We hadn't talked much.

605
00:24:22,528 --> 00:24:24,463
But I asked you so many questions.

606
00:24:24,463 --> 00:24:25,564
Did you?

607
00:24:25,564 --> 00:24:27,566
I asked you quite a few too.

608
00:24:27,566 --> 00:24:29,368
I made such an effort to talk to you.

609
00:24:29,368 --> 00:24:30,402
Really?

610
00:24:32,471 --> 00:24:34,072
I brought this up too.

611
00:24:34,072 --> 00:24:35,240
And the rolled omelet.

612
00:24:35,741 --> 00:24:37,242
The omelet,

613
00:24:37,242 --> 00:24:39,645
and asking if you wanted
to go grocery shopping.

614
00:24:39,645 --> 00:24:40,846
Now that you mention it, you're right.

615
00:24:40,846 --> 00:24:42,447
I really did talk to you a lot.

616
00:24:42,848 --> 00:24:44,316
(Laughs)

617
00:24:44,950 --> 00:24:45,884
Seriously.

618
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:52,991
(He films Min Young in her uniform
with the vintage camcorder.)

619
00:24:55,694 --> 00:24:59,031
- Is this the vibe?
- Yes, it has a cool vibe.

620
00:24:59,932 --> 00:25:01,066
Where should I shoot?

621
00:25:01,867 --> 00:25:02,901
Come over here.

622
00:25:04,169 --> 00:25:05,070
This looks lovely.

623
00:25:05,571 --> 00:25:06,405
Cool.

624
00:25:06,405 --> 00:25:08,273
Wait. This looks like a music video.

625
00:25:08,273 --> 00:25:09,541
- A music video.
- It really does.

626
00:25:09,541 --> 00:25:11,109
Stay in the middle...

627
00:25:11,677 --> 00:25:12,477
(Laughs)

628
00:25:12,778 --> 00:25:15,914
(He means a NewJeans music video.)

629
00:25:19,284 --> 00:25:20,586
Here, this street!

630
00:25:21,386 --> 00:25:23,155
This street looks pretty.

631
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:25,524
- Smile.
- I'll film you.

632
00:25:25,524 --> 00:25:27,893
Let it shake a little. Smile.

633
00:25:27,893 --> 00:25:28,827
Look over here.

634
00:25:31,930 --> 00:25:32,865
Why is it so blurry?

635
00:25:33,799 --> 00:25:35,601
- Try harder.
- Okay.

636
00:25:39,004 --> 00:25:41,540
Keep filming. It's pretty. I'll get you.

637
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:42,774
Okay, take the umbrella.

638
00:25:42,774 --> 00:25:43,809
The umbrella is fine.

639
00:25:44,343 --> 00:25:46,211
Wait, we're backlit.

640
00:25:49,448 --> 00:25:51,650
Smile. Look here and keep smiling.

641
00:25:54,019 --> 00:25:55,187
(Close together)

642
00:25:56,655 --> 00:25:57,556
Got it.

643
00:25:58,290 --> 00:25:59,892
The mirror. The glass.

644
00:26:00,859 --> 00:26:02,861
The glass. One, two, three.

645
00:26:02,861 --> 00:26:04,029
Can you see us, though?

646
00:26:04,029 --> 00:26:04,830
Yeah.

647
00:26:05,464 --> 00:26:07,633
We need to take this off.

648
00:26:07,633 --> 00:26:08,767
(They film each other from up close.)

649
00:26:17,242 --> 00:26:19,778
They're adorable. What is this?

650
00:26:19,778 --> 00:26:21,580
This must feel so romantic.

651
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:22,781
They already look like a couple.

652
00:26:22,781 --> 00:26:24,049
Exactly.

653
00:26:24,049 --> 00:26:26,718
Her whole body is turned toward him.

654
00:26:27,386 --> 00:26:29,821
- She must really like him.
- Exactly.

655
00:26:29,821 --> 00:26:30,956
You can tell.

656
00:26:30,956 --> 00:26:31,990
She's a schoolgirl again.

657
00:26:31,990 --> 00:26:33,425
We can feel it from the studio.

658
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:34,493
(Excited)

659
00:26:34,793 --> 00:26:35,794
By the way...

660
00:26:35,794 --> 00:26:36,662
Yeah?

661
00:26:36,662 --> 00:26:37,696
Do you like spicy rice cakes?

662
00:26:37,696 --> 00:26:38,564
Spicy rice cakes?

663
00:26:38,564 --> 00:26:40,365
- I love it.
- Really?

664
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:44,870
(They reach
Min Young's spicy rice cakes spot.)

665
00:26:46,438 --> 00:26:48,006
Hello.

666
00:26:48,006 --> 00:26:48,974
Hello.

667
00:26:50,776 --> 00:26:52,077
I was just getting hungry.

668
00:26:52,077 --> 00:26:53,178
Really?

669
00:26:53,512 --> 00:26:54,646
How do I look?

670
00:26:54,646 --> 00:26:56,281
It looks great. You look younger.

671
00:26:56,281 --> 00:26:57,282
Do I look like a student?

672
00:26:57,282 --> 00:26:58,917
You really look like a student.

673
00:26:58,917 --> 00:27:00,152
Well, maybe,

674
00:27:00,152 --> 00:27:02,521
I did think you looked like an adult
in a school uniform.

675
00:27:02,521 --> 00:27:03,856
(Laughs)

676
00:27:04,323 --> 00:27:05,424
But also like a student.

677
00:27:05,424 --> 00:27:07,125
It suits you. Navy really works on you.

678
00:27:07,125 --> 00:27:08,126
Really?

679
00:27:08,126 --> 00:27:08,994
Thank you.

680
00:27:08,994 --> 00:27:10,195
(Laughs)

681
00:27:11,396 --> 00:27:14,766
It's my first time wearing one
as an adult.

682
00:27:14,766 --> 00:27:16,001
It looks great on you.

683
00:27:16,335 --> 00:27:17,803
(Shy)

684
00:27:18,203 --> 00:27:19,571
(The spicy rice cakes arrive.)

685
00:27:19,571 --> 00:27:20,706
Thank you.

686
00:27:22,074 --> 00:27:23,175
It looks delicious.

687
00:27:26,778 --> 00:27:27,846
Would you like some water?

688
00:27:27,846 --> 00:27:28,647
Yes.

689
00:27:30,749 --> 00:27:31,416
(Ding)

690
00:27:32,217 --> 00:27:33,952
- That came out well.
- Really?

691
00:27:33,952 --> 00:27:35,254
Smile.

692
00:27:35,254 --> 00:27:36,154
(V-sign)

693
00:27:37,556 --> 00:27:38,790
You really look like a student.

694
00:27:41,393 --> 00:27:42,628
Did you press record?

695
00:27:43,862 --> 00:27:45,264
I thought you hit record
before giving it to me.

696
00:27:46,231 --> 00:27:47,766
(Silent laughter)

697
00:27:50,602 --> 00:27:51,537
Come closer.

698
00:27:52,104 --> 00:27:53,505
Roar.

699
00:27:54,406 --> 00:27:55,674
Good.

700
00:27:55,674 --> 00:27:57,576
But the way we turn off the camera...

701
00:27:57,576 --> 00:27:59,478
looks really awkward.

702
00:27:59,478 --> 00:28:00,279
Did you turn it off?

703
00:28:00,279 --> 00:28:01,580
You didn't turn it off.

704
00:28:02,181 --> 00:28:04,950
It won't look cinematic.

705
00:28:05,851 --> 00:28:07,953
But that has its own charm.

706
00:28:07,953 --> 00:28:08,987
I'll serve you some.

707
00:28:08,987 --> 00:28:10,923
- Thank you.
- That's part of the charm.

708
00:28:10,923 --> 00:28:12,257
What do you like in it?

709
00:28:12,257 --> 00:28:13,292
I like everything.

710
00:28:14,626 --> 00:28:16,128
The rice cakes are huge.

711
00:28:19,898 --> 00:28:20,999
Thank you.

712
00:28:23,435 --> 00:28:24,403
(Plop)

713
00:28:25,504 --> 00:28:26,638
Did you spill anything?

714
00:28:26,638 --> 00:28:27,506
No, I didn't.

715
00:28:27,506 --> 00:28:28,540
You didn't spill it?

716
00:28:29,675 --> 00:28:30,709
(Takes a bite)

717
00:28:31,610 --> 00:28:32,544
Is it good?

718
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:33,412
Yeah.

719
00:28:37,883 --> 00:28:41,587
When did your hospital stays begin?

720
00:28:41,920 --> 00:28:45,290
When I was 14, early that year.

721
00:28:45,290 --> 00:28:46,859
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

722
00:28:47,593 --> 00:28:48,560
Until I was 15.

723
00:28:48,827 --> 00:28:50,329
From 14 to 15?

724
00:28:50,762 --> 00:28:52,030
I had surgery every year.

725
00:28:52,030 --> 00:28:54,099
I had surgery through tenth grade.

726
00:28:54,099 --> 00:28:55,767
What about school?

727
00:28:56,468 --> 00:28:59,404
I went to school online in middle school.

728
00:28:59,404 --> 00:29:02,307
I returned in person late in eighth grade.

729
00:29:02,774 --> 00:29:05,377
Then COVID-19 hit.

730
00:29:05,377 --> 00:29:06,311
You were sick during the pandemic, right?

731
00:29:06,311 --> 00:29:07,746
- Yes.
- Right?

732
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:09,581
I was getting a little better by then.

733
00:29:10,782 --> 00:29:13,485
During the pandemic, I was...

734
00:29:14,119 --> 00:29:15,354
in the military.

735
00:29:15,354 --> 00:29:17,055
So you were a student during COVID-19?

736
00:29:17,055 --> 00:29:19,024
(She slips up.)

737
00:29:19,024 --> 00:29:20,092
Now I know.

738
00:29:21,026 --> 00:29:22,327
(She accidentally reveals her age.)

739
00:29:22,327 --> 00:29:23,529
I have a rough idea now.

740
00:29:23,529 --> 00:29:24,930
But I could've been...

741
00:29:25,397 --> 00:29:26,899
A college student.

742
00:29:29,201 --> 00:29:31,136
Anyway, that's what happened.

743
00:29:31,136 --> 00:29:34,406
So after COVID-19 hit,

744
00:29:34,406 --> 00:29:36,475
were you able to attend school?

745
00:29:37,042 --> 00:29:38,143
I did,

746
00:29:38,143 --> 00:29:41,513
but I don't really remember graduation.

747
00:29:41,513 --> 00:29:44,216
No school trip stands out either.

748
00:29:44,583 --> 00:29:47,452
I even missed...

749
00:29:47,452 --> 00:29:50,255
my elementary school graduation.

750
00:29:50,255 --> 00:29:53,659
You were sick in your most active years.

751
00:29:54,126 --> 00:29:55,060
So that's why...

752
00:29:55,961 --> 00:29:57,596
I chose uniforms and spicy rice cakes.

753
00:29:58,330 --> 00:29:59,565
Now I get it.

754
00:29:59,565 --> 00:30:01,333
You understand how I felt, right?

755
00:30:01,333 --> 00:30:02,434
I think I do.

756
00:30:03,402 --> 00:30:05,437
When you've been seriously ill,

757
00:30:05,437 --> 00:30:07,773
bucket-list dreams aren't grand, are they?

758
00:30:07,773 --> 00:30:11,376
Maybe you learn to cherish simple things.

759
00:30:11,376 --> 00:30:13,478
You wonder what you wanted to do,

760
00:30:13,478 --> 00:30:16,415
and it's as simple as taking a walk.

761
00:30:16,415 --> 00:30:17,583
Right.

762
00:30:17,583 --> 00:30:18,750
I think that's true for everyone here.

763
00:30:20,853 --> 00:30:24,156
You said that whenever you talked to me,

764
00:30:24,156 --> 00:30:27,092
my tone was a little stiff.

765
00:30:27,092 --> 00:30:29,461
When we discussed first impressions,

766
00:30:29,962 --> 00:30:31,563
I thought I'd offended you.

767
00:30:31,563 --> 00:30:33,232
What did you say again?

768
00:30:33,799 --> 00:30:35,901
I meant a different kind of cloud.

769
00:30:37,636 --> 00:30:40,405
When you first walked in,

770
00:30:40,739 --> 00:30:42,374
you reminded me of a cloud.

771
00:30:42,374 --> 00:30:44,276
Something soft and fluffy.

772
00:30:44,276 --> 00:30:45,978
A cloud? Thanks.

773
00:30:47,045 --> 00:30:48,247
Min Young, you were incredibly quiet.

774
00:30:48,514 --> 00:30:50,182
You were a different kind of cloud.

775
00:30:50,182 --> 00:30:51,850
- What?
- I could barely hear your steps.

776
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:52,684
That kind of quiet.

777
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:55,053
I meant you were that quiet.

778
00:30:55,287 --> 00:30:57,489
What does "quiet like a cloud" mean?

779
00:30:58,390 --> 00:30:59,925
(Flustered)

780
00:30:59,925 --> 00:31:01,460
That put me on the spot.

781
00:31:01,460 --> 00:31:02,828
You felt put on the spot?

782
00:31:03,462 --> 00:31:05,998
(Min Young didn't realize how he felt.)

783
00:31:05,998 --> 00:31:07,633
If that happened again,

784
00:31:07,633 --> 00:31:09,835
I didn't think I could handle it.

785
00:31:09,835 --> 00:31:12,671
I'd want the ground to swallow me up.

786
00:31:12,671 --> 00:31:13,505
So I thought I should be careful.

787
00:31:13,505 --> 00:31:14,640
Since you're an INFP,

788
00:31:14,640 --> 00:31:16,909
I tried to react differently to you.

789
00:31:16,909 --> 00:31:20,479
I meant, "You're funny, Seon Ho."

790
00:31:20,479 --> 00:31:21,747
And that put you on the spot.

791
00:31:21,747 --> 00:31:23,515
(Flustered)

792
00:31:24,316 --> 00:31:25,817
I just...

793
00:31:26,318 --> 00:31:30,989
No one's said I put them on the spot.

794
00:31:30,989 --> 00:31:33,358
I'm shocked right now.

795
00:31:33,358 --> 00:31:34,626
It was probably how you phrased it.

796
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:38,063
(Min Young can't hide her embarrassment.)

797
00:31:41,233 --> 00:31:43,535
I'd have broken out in a cold sweat too.

798
00:31:43,535 --> 00:31:45,337
If I were Min Young,

799
00:31:45,337 --> 00:31:48,874
I'd realize, "So that's how I sounded."

800
00:31:48,874 --> 00:31:51,410
I'd feel awful and start sweating.

801
00:31:51,410 --> 00:31:54,346
You'd worry that he thought...

802
00:31:54,346 --> 00:31:55,647
you were being mean to him.

803
00:31:55,647 --> 00:31:59,151
It made the mood feel subtly awkward.

804
00:31:59,151 --> 00:32:00,419
Their timing was slightly off.

805
00:32:00,419 --> 00:32:01,620
I think they were a little out of sync.

806
00:32:01,620 --> 00:32:03,655
- I think so too.
- Exactly.

807
00:32:05,357 --> 00:32:08,660
I figured that's just how you talk.

808
00:32:08,660 --> 00:32:09,928
That was my takeaway.

809
00:32:09,928 --> 00:32:12,064
You didn't mean anything by it,

810
00:32:12,064 --> 00:32:16,101
but it caught me off guard.

811
00:32:16,101 --> 00:32:18,170
I didn't know how to respond.

812
00:32:19,171 --> 00:32:21,707
So that's what happened.

813
00:32:21,707 --> 00:32:23,675
I had no idea.

814
00:32:28,847 --> 00:32:29,948
Anyway,

815
00:32:31,016 --> 00:32:34,052
I was trying to treat you specially.

816
00:32:34,786 --> 00:32:35,821
Really.

817
00:32:35,821 --> 00:32:36,955
Thank you.

818
00:32:36,955 --> 00:32:38,524
You were trying to be thoughtful.

819
00:32:38,524 --> 00:32:39,925
That's all I was trying to do.

820
00:32:39,925 --> 00:32:44,062
I didn't know I'd come off so stiff.

821
00:32:49,835 --> 00:32:53,105
(The date lasts for your combined time.)

822
00:32:53,105 --> 00:32:57,509
(Kang Min Young and Kim Seon Ho,
your 100-minute date has ended.)

823
00:32:58,410 --> 00:32:59,611
(Min Young 100 minutes,
Seon Ho 0 minutes)

824
00:32:59,611 --> 00:33:01,980
- Did you see the text?
- Yes.

825
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:03,782
We barely got any footage.

826
00:33:03,782 --> 00:33:04,883
Exactly.

827
00:33:05,717 --> 00:33:07,052
Let's get some shots in.

828
00:33:07,052 --> 00:33:08,820
Get a few shots before we leave. Hurry.

829
00:33:13,625 --> 00:33:15,961
It fell a little short...

830
00:33:15,961 --> 00:33:17,496
of what I'd hoped for.

831
00:33:17,496 --> 00:33:21,333
It was my first date with Seon Ho...

832
00:33:21,333 --> 00:33:24,069
and really our first real conversation.

833
00:33:24,069 --> 00:33:25,671
I really enjoyed the date itself.

834
00:33:25,671 --> 00:33:27,506
I don't regret going on it at all.

835
00:33:28,307 --> 00:33:29,641
I'll film on the way back too.

836
00:33:29,641 --> 00:33:32,177
(Can they close the 100-minute gap?)

837
00:33:34,780 --> 00:33:40,752
(They film each other one last time.)

838
00:33:41,653 --> 00:33:43,121
- Got it?
- Yeah.

839
00:33:43,121 --> 00:33:44,022
The end.

840
00:33:44,423 --> 00:33:45,290
The end.

841
00:33:45,624 --> 00:33:47,125
And let's film as we walk.

842
00:33:52,064 --> 00:33:53,198
- Ready?
- Yes.

843
00:33:53,198 --> 00:33:55,400
(Kim Seon Ho,
your second date is waiting.)

844
00:33:59,972 --> 00:34:01,406
(Their date ends on an uncertain note.)

845
00:34:01,406 --> 00:34:03,742
We talked so much, we barely ate.

846
00:34:03,742 --> 00:34:04,910
Are you full?

847
00:34:04,910 --> 00:34:07,179
I eat small meals pretty often.

848
00:34:10,382 --> 00:34:11,917
(Meanwhile)

849
00:34:11,917 --> 00:34:13,018
Thank you.

850
00:34:13,552 --> 00:34:15,654
My stomach won't stop growling.

851
00:34:15,654 --> 00:34:16,688
Really? I didn't hear it.

852
00:34:16,688 --> 00:34:17,923
You can't hear it?

853
00:34:17,923 --> 00:34:19,157
No, I can't.

854
00:34:20,025 --> 00:34:21,994
It's growling like crazy.

855
00:34:21,994 --> 00:34:23,595
Mine was too.

856
00:34:23,595 --> 00:34:24,663
- Really?
- Yes.

857
00:34:25,297 --> 00:34:26,265
Do I add it like this?

858
00:34:26,265 --> 00:34:27,833
Yes, just like that.

859
00:34:27,833 --> 00:34:28,901
It's so warm.

860
00:34:29,167 --> 00:34:30,335
Really warm.

861
00:34:32,337 --> 00:34:33,338
(Glances)

862
00:34:34,339 --> 00:34:35,440
Is this enough?

863
00:34:37,976 --> 00:34:39,645
- Enjoy.
- Enjoy.

864
00:34:41,113 --> 00:34:42,147
(Tries the soup)

865
00:34:42,981 --> 00:34:44,016
How is it?

866
00:34:44,449 --> 00:34:45,584
It's good.

867
00:34:45,851 --> 00:34:46,919
- Really?
- Yes.

868
00:34:47,619 --> 00:34:48,453
Why?

869
00:34:48,954 --> 00:34:50,856
I haven't tried it yet.

870
00:34:51,456 --> 00:34:53,325
Do you like ochazuke?

871
00:34:53,325 --> 00:34:55,327
I love it.

872
00:34:56,562 --> 00:34:59,565
(They share Ro Bin's favorite meal.)

873
00:35:01,867 --> 00:35:03,001
(Glances)

874
00:35:03,468 --> 00:35:06,104
Do you really have something to ask?

875
00:35:10,542 --> 00:35:11,543
I do.

876
00:35:14,246 --> 00:35:15,714
(Reads the room)

877
00:35:16,281 --> 00:35:17,416
Looking ahead,

878
00:35:18,383 --> 00:35:19,284
we have...

879
00:35:19,985 --> 00:35:21,920
about four days left, right?

880
00:35:23,689 --> 00:35:25,824
What are you planning to do?

881
00:35:26,491 --> 00:35:27,726
About what?

882
00:35:28,460 --> 00:35:31,864
How you'll get to know everyone.

883
00:35:32,631 --> 00:35:36,001
After talking to several people,

884
00:35:36,001 --> 00:35:39,471
I think I'll focus on one person.

885
00:35:44,943 --> 00:35:46,979
But...

886
00:35:46,979 --> 00:35:49,982
you were the only one I hadn't talked to.

887
00:35:50,582 --> 00:35:51,583
That's understandable.

888
00:35:52,217 --> 00:35:54,353
Does it take you a while to warm up?

889
00:35:54,353 --> 00:35:56,321
- I think so.
- I see.

890
00:35:56,321 --> 00:35:59,091
If I spend enough time with someone,

891
00:35:59,091 --> 00:36:01,894
I warm up to them faster.

892
00:36:01,894 --> 00:36:02,861
So...

893
00:36:04,363 --> 00:36:06,598
that's why time together matters.

894
00:36:06,598 --> 00:36:08,033
Right.

895
00:36:08,033 --> 00:36:09,701
- That's what I thought.
- Me too.

896
00:36:11,136 --> 00:36:14,139
I kept wondering how Jong Eun felt.

897
00:36:14,139 --> 00:36:16,341
Was he happy? Did his heart race?

898
00:36:17,609 --> 00:36:19,244
Was he bored?

899
00:36:19,244 --> 00:36:21,680
Was it too quiet and low-key?

900
00:36:22,781 --> 00:36:24,616
I kept...

901
00:36:24,616 --> 00:36:27,219
focusing so much...

902
00:36:27,219 --> 00:36:29,588
on how the other person felt.

903
00:36:31,723 --> 00:36:32,925
That's so sad.

904
00:36:32,925 --> 00:36:35,093
(They feel for her.)

905
00:36:35,093 --> 00:36:36,461
I can see why she'd feel that way.

906
00:36:37,930 --> 00:36:41,099
She's not just caught up in her feelings.

907
00:36:41,099 --> 00:36:43,035
She knows their time is precious.

908
00:36:43,035 --> 00:36:44,937
But Ro Bin really gave it her all.

909
00:36:44,937 --> 00:36:46,371
She tried so hard.

910
00:36:46,805 --> 00:36:48,473
You could see how badly she wanted this.

911
00:36:48,974 --> 00:36:50,542
- This is so hard.
- Yes.

912
00:36:51,276 --> 00:36:52,144
It's hard.

913
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:57,616
(This time together)

914
00:36:57,616 --> 00:37:01,153
(What does it mean to each of them?)

915
00:37:01,954 --> 00:37:05,290
(Their time is nearly up.)

916
00:37:05,290 --> 00:37:07,392
I'm full now.

917
00:37:07,392 --> 00:37:09,595
The portion is pretty big, right?

918
00:37:09,595 --> 00:37:12,030
The rice swelled after adding water.

919
00:37:12,998 --> 00:37:14,233
There's more...

920
00:37:14,800 --> 00:37:15,567
Than we expected.

921
00:37:15,567 --> 00:37:17,035
It looks small, but there's a ton.

922
00:37:17,035 --> 00:37:17,903
Exactly.

923
00:37:26,325 --> 00:37:28,760
(The date lasts for your combined time.)

924
00:37:28,760 --> 00:37:30,429
(Seo Ro Bin and Kim Jong Eun,
your 100-minute date has ended.)

925
00:37:30,429 --> 00:37:33,398
(Jong Eun, 0 min / Ro Bin, 100 min)

926
00:37:36,535 --> 00:37:39,238
So this is how you find out.

927
00:37:40,372 --> 00:37:43,141
I was happy and grateful,

928
00:37:43,141 --> 00:37:44,343
but at the same time,

929
00:37:44,343 --> 00:37:47,946
I also felt guilty.

930
00:37:50,048 --> 00:37:55,287
It said, "Your 100-minute date has ended."

931
00:37:56,255 --> 00:37:58,423
Part of me expected it,

932
00:37:58,423 --> 00:37:59,925
but it still meant...

933
00:37:59,925 --> 00:38:03,095
he didn't want to spend...

934
00:38:03,762 --> 00:38:04,796
even ten minutes on me.

935
00:38:04,796 --> 00:38:06,231
It hit me...

936
00:38:06,231 --> 00:38:08,500
that I had no place in Jong Eun's heart.

937
00:38:08,500 --> 00:38:10,035
That text made it feel...

938
00:38:10,035 --> 00:38:12,471
painfully real.

939
00:38:13,939 --> 00:38:16,208
And that...

940
00:38:16,208 --> 00:38:18,010
really hurt.

941
00:38:25,250 --> 00:38:26,418
How was it?

942
00:38:30,189 --> 00:38:31,156
Thank you.

943
00:38:34,059 --> 00:38:34,927
Sure.

944
00:38:35,928 --> 00:38:36,829
(Dumbfounded)

945
00:38:36,829 --> 00:38:38,597
For what?

946
00:38:38,597 --> 00:38:40,165
"Thank you for spending your time on me."

947
00:38:41,834 --> 00:38:43,068
(Laughs)

948
00:38:43,068 --> 00:38:45,571
Because Jong Eun only sees Min Young.

949
00:38:45,571 --> 00:38:47,039
Right, for now.

950
00:38:47,039 --> 00:38:49,007
He can't think about anyone else yet.

951
00:38:49,007 --> 00:38:50,475
- No one else interests him.
- Exactly.

952
00:38:50,475 --> 00:38:51,310
He just doesn't have...

953
00:38:51,310 --> 00:38:52,744
Room for anyone else. That's right.

954
00:38:52,744 --> 00:38:56,081
Look at how he's lived.

955
00:38:56,081 --> 00:38:58,617
He's been laser-focused on firefighting.

956
00:38:58,617 --> 00:39:00,185
Once he's committed, he goes all in.

957
00:39:00,185 --> 00:39:01,620
Right. He goes straight for it.

958
00:39:01,620 --> 00:39:04,289
No one is at fault here.

959
00:39:04,289 --> 00:39:06,058
Jong Eun isn't a bad guy at all.

960
00:39:06,058 --> 00:39:07,526
Not at all.

961
00:39:07,526 --> 00:39:09,695
He did the best he could.

962
00:39:09,695 --> 00:39:10,762
A man who knows what he wants.

963
00:39:12,564 --> 00:39:14,032
How was it?

964
00:39:14,032 --> 00:39:14,900
Me?

965
00:39:15,434 --> 00:39:18,971
I honestly never saw it coming.

966
00:39:20,439 --> 00:39:21,707
And...

967
00:39:21,707 --> 00:39:24,610
I truly hadn't noticed your signals.

968
00:39:25,744 --> 00:39:29,147
(Ro Bin's feelings didn't reach Jong Eun.)

969
00:39:30,782 --> 00:39:33,018
That's the impression I'd had.

970
00:39:33,018 --> 00:39:38,690
I wanted to get to know everyone anyway.

971
00:39:38,690 --> 00:39:42,961
I just started with my top two.

972
00:39:43,328 --> 00:39:45,998
- You started with your favorites.
- Yes.

973
00:39:46,532 --> 00:39:49,635
(Jong Eun says she wasn't a priority.)

974
00:39:50,769 --> 00:39:52,304
If we get another date...

975
00:39:57,242 --> 00:39:58,844
So I wasn't even worth ten minutes.

976
00:39:58,844 --> 00:40:00,546
That's not...

977
00:40:00,546 --> 00:40:01,914
- Okay.
- No.

978
00:40:02,414 --> 00:40:04,483
(Kim Jong Eun,
your second date is waiting.)

979
00:40:04,483 --> 00:40:06,051
(Please move to the next location.)

980
00:40:06,552 --> 00:40:08,086
(Hurt)

981
00:40:11,356 --> 00:40:13,358
I'll get going.

982
00:40:21,366 --> 00:40:23,569
- You should take your jacket.
- Right.

983
00:40:24,503 --> 00:40:25,804
(She gives back Jong Eun's warm jacket.)

984
00:40:25,804 --> 00:40:26,705
I'm sorry.

985
00:40:26,705 --> 00:40:28,006
Why are you sorry?

986
00:40:28,006 --> 00:40:29,141
What are you sorry for?

987
00:40:32,477 --> 00:40:34,279
- I'll get going.
- Take care.

988
00:40:40,185 --> 00:40:44,189
(Ro Bin and Jong Eun's
100-minute date ends.)

989
00:40:46,692 --> 00:40:50,896
I think that text hit me so hard...

990
00:40:50,896 --> 00:40:52,965
that I don't remember what happened after.

991
00:40:55,567 --> 00:41:00,272
(Her long-awaited time
with Jong Eun ends.)

992
00:41:05,744 --> 00:41:08,480
(Seo Ro Bin, your second date is waiting.)

993
00:41:08,480 --> 00:41:10,716
(Please move to the next location.)

994
00:41:14,520 --> 00:41:19,358
(Where will Ro Bin's time take her next?)

995
00:41:20,159 --> 00:41:22,361
(Gyeongui Line Forest Park)

996
00:41:24,229 --> 00:41:25,597
(Nervous)

997
00:41:26,899 --> 00:41:31,236
(Na Young is about to meet Do Gon.)

998
00:41:31,970 --> 00:41:33,305
Our team leader.

999
00:41:34,273 --> 00:41:36,441
It's been too long, Team Leader.

1000
00:41:36,441 --> 00:41:37,576
(Thrilled)

1001
00:41:37,576 --> 00:41:38,977
Let's give it up for her.

1002
00:41:38,977 --> 00:41:40,746
The team leader finally has a date.

1003
00:41:40,746 --> 00:41:41,547
Finally.

1004
00:41:42,314 --> 00:41:44,116
- I can't wait for this.
- Me neither.

1005
00:41:44,116 --> 00:41:46,151
I think this couple looks good together.

1006
00:41:46,151 --> 00:41:48,053
- They're my favorite pairing.
- Great match.

1007
00:41:48,053 --> 00:41:50,889
They feel like a social-powerhouse couple.

1008
00:41:50,889 --> 00:41:52,524
- Right?
- Exactly.

1009
00:41:52,524 --> 00:41:55,160
It's a proper grown-up date.

1010
00:41:55,160 --> 00:41:56,395
That's what it feels like.

1011
00:41:57,296 --> 00:42:00,499
(Butterflies before meeting Do Gon)

1012
00:42:07,239 --> 00:42:08,974
(Spots him)

1013
00:42:10,876 --> 00:42:12,311
(Grins)

1014
00:42:14,012 --> 00:42:15,080
My goodness.

1015
00:42:23,889 --> 00:42:24,857
Hello.

1016
00:42:26,358 --> 00:42:27,426
Cool.

1017
00:42:28,126 --> 00:42:29,161
Hello.

1018
00:42:30,562 --> 00:42:31,563
Cool.

1019
00:42:32,030 --> 00:42:33,665
- What?
- Our outfits almost match.

1020
00:42:34,333 --> 00:42:35,167
(Unexpected matching outfits)

1021
00:42:35,167 --> 00:42:36,768
You're right. They do.

1022
00:42:38,704 --> 00:42:40,305
You didn't see my outfit, did you?

1023
00:42:40,939 --> 00:42:41,740
No.

1024
00:42:42,808 --> 00:42:44,910
(A thrilling coincidence)

1025
00:42:44,910 --> 00:42:51,517
(Do Gon and Na Young's
100-minute date begins.)

1026
00:42:52,518 --> 00:42:55,787
I haven't walked around here in ages.

1027
00:42:55,787 --> 00:42:57,089
Have you been this way before?

1028
00:42:57,089 --> 00:42:58,590
I used to wander around here...

1029
00:42:58,590 --> 00:43:00,159
every now and then.

1030
00:43:08,467 --> 00:43:09,668
Is this the place?

1031
00:43:11,937 --> 00:43:14,006
Watch your step coming down.

1032
00:43:15,874 --> 00:43:16,975
A studio.

1033
00:43:17,809 --> 00:43:18,944
(Startled)

1034
00:43:19,778 --> 00:43:20,913
- No way.
- No way.

1035
00:43:23,549 --> 00:43:24,616
I see.

1036
00:43:25,250 --> 00:43:26,151
Music?

1037
00:43:29,555 --> 00:43:32,591
(Listening to music I truly love)

1038
00:43:32,591 --> 00:43:35,594
(And eating meat I love outdoors)

1039
00:43:35,594 --> 00:43:38,297
Before I got sick,

1040
00:43:38,297 --> 00:43:40,299
I always fell asleep with earbuds in.

1041
00:43:40,299 --> 00:43:41,133
I did it so much...

1042
00:43:41,133 --> 00:43:42,768
that my mom would scold me.

1043
00:43:42,768 --> 00:43:44,336
"You'll damage your hearing."

1044
00:43:45,237 --> 00:43:46,438
Since I can't do that anymore,

1045
00:43:48,207 --> 00:43:51,777
I started liking vinyl bars...

1046
00:43:51,777 --> 00:43:54,446
and places with live music.

1047
00:43:55,280 --> 00:43:56,915
Ideally, I'd like someone...

1048
00:43:56,915 --> 00:43:59,418
who enjoys the same things.

1049
00:43:59,418 --> 00:44:01,353
I was curious if he'd like this too.

1050
00:44:02,821 --> 00:44:05,591
(Na Young's bucket list, a vinyl bar date)

1051
00:44:06,859 --> 00:44:07,993
How do you like the vibe?

1052
00:44:07,993 --> 00:44:09,161
I love it.

1053
00:44:09,928 --> 00:44:12,097
Why don't we each...

1054
00:44:12,097 --> 00:44:13,265
pick a song?

1055
00:44:13,899 --> 00:44:15,467
Pick one vinyl record each?

1056
00:44:17,369 --> 00:44:21,807
(Sharing their taste in music)

1057
00:44:23,642 --> 00:44:25,077
(Tap)

1058
00:44:26,378 --> 00:44:28,881
Rainy days make me think of...

1059
00:44:28,881 --> 00:44:30,015
Lee Moon Sae.

1060
00:44:30,015 --> 00:44:30,816
I love him.

1061
00:44:30,816 --> 00:44:33,018
Kim Hyun Sik and Lee Moon Sae.

1062
00:44:34,186 --> 00:44:37,089
(They share the same taste in music.)

1063
00:44:37,523 --> 00:44:38,857
I like Lee So Ra too.

1064
00:44:40,125 --> 00:44:41,260
Do you like Lee So Ra?

1065
00:44:41,260 --> 00:44:42,828
Yes, I love her.

1066
00:44:44,530 --> 00:44:45,898
Lee So Ra's greatest hits.

1067
00:44:46,231 --> 00:44:47,299
(Gently)

1068
00:44:49,001 --> 00:44:50,869
What was that?

1069
00:44:50,869 --> 00:44:51,737
(Heart fluttering)

1070
00:44:51,737 --> 00:44:54,306
I love moments like this.

1071
00:44:54,306 --> 00:44:55,841
Wait.

1072
00:44:55,841 --> 00:44:57,209
Hold on.

1073
00:44:57,209 --> 00:44:59,111
Who filmed that angle?

1074
00:44:59,444 --> 00:45:00,879
That was such a great shot.

1075
00:45:00,879 --> 00:45:01,847
I love it.

1076
00:45:07,085 --> 00:45:09,788
There are two vinyl records.

1077
00:45:09,788 --> 00:45:10,822
In here?

1078
00:45:10,822 --> 00:45:12,791
(Their first shared pick is Lee So Ra.)

1079
00:45:12,791 --> 00:45:13,859
Cool.

1080
00:45:16,261 --> 00:45:22,067
(They put on the vinyl
they chose together.)

1081
00:45:25,270 --> 00:45:26,772
(Up close)

1082
00:45:27,005 --> 00:45:27,873
Lift it.

1083
00:45:40,886 --> 00:45:42,988
Nice. Do you know "Confession?"

1084
00:45:42,988 --> 00:45:43,956
Of course.

1085
00:45:50,028 --> 00:45:54,633
("Confession" by Lee So Ra)

1086
00:45:56,401 --> 00:45:58,303
- I love this place.
- Such a great song.

1087
00:46:00,339 --> 00:46:06,044
(They listen to their chosen song.)

1088
00:46:09,014 --> 00:46:10,082
Honestly,

1089
00:46:11,216 --> 00:46:12,885
I couldn't read you at all.

1090
00:46:12,885 --> 00:46:14,953
Me? You mean my personality?

1091
00:46:14,953 --> 00:46:15,787
Yes.

1092
00:46:16,955 --> 00:46:18,323
Because...

1093
00:46:19,358 --> 00:46:21,927
you're the quietest person here,

1094
00:46:22,694 --> 00:46:23,829
and you seemed...

1095
00:46:23,829 --> 00:46:28,033
like my complete opposite.

1096
00:46:30,102 --> 00:46:31,570
So honestly,

1097
00:46:31,570 --> 00:46:34,006
I wasn't sure how to approach you.

1098
00:46:34,006 --> 00:46:39,478
I thought I might overwhelm you.

1099
00:46:40,579 --> 00:46:41,847
So I wanted to know more.

1100
00:46:44,116 --> 00:46:47,486
(Curious about someone unlike herself)

1101
00:46:48,253 --> 00:46:50,589
That doesn't bother me at all.

1102
00:46:51,256 --> 00:46:53,458
I have some really high-energy friends.

1103
00:46:53,458 --> 00:46:57,129
I'm surrounded by people like that.

1104
00:46:57,129 --> 00:47:00,732
Maybe we balance each other out.

1105
00:47:02,100 --> 00:47:04,670
Even when it comes to dating,

1106
00:47:06,738 --> 00:47:10,108
I've always thought
differences can be a good thing.

1107
00:47:10,108 --> 00:47:12,511
You've thought about it,
but never tried it.

1108
00:47:12,511 --> 00:47:13,412
Right.

1109
00:47:14,413 --> 00:47:15,647
What do you think I'd be like to date?

1110
00:47:16,481 --> 00:47:18,483
(Na Young's straightforward question)

1111
00:47:18,483 --> 00:47:20,552
(Butterflies)

1112
00:47:20,552 --> 00:47:21,386
My gosh.

1113
00:47:21,386 --> 00:47:22,287
She went straight for it.

1114
00:47:22,287 --> 00:47:23,589
Is the music getting to her?

1115
00:47:24,356 --> 00:47:26,425
Hold on. Ye Na's practically...

1116
00:47:26,425 --> 00:47:28,160
(Completely immersed)

1117
00:47:28,160 --> 00:47:30,629
- Look at her.
- Is she in that vinyl bar?

1118
00:47:30,629 --> 00:47:31,964
This is perfect.

1119
00:47:34,099 --> 00:47:35,634
(Surprised)

1120
00:47:36,668 --> 00:47:38,070
Honestly,

1121
00:47:38,070 --> 00:47:41,807
I've always liked people similar to me.

1122
00:47:42,808 --> 00:47:43,742
But then again,

1123
00:47:43,742 --> 00:47:46,011
I'd also like to date someone...

1124
00:47:47,646 --> 00:47:48,914
with the opposite personality.

1125
00:47:50,415 --> 00:47:53,185
(As they get to know each other,)

1126
00:47:53,185 --> 00:47:56,922
(their curiosity grows.)

1127
00:47:56,922 --> 00:48:00,159
The person I was most curious about...

1128
00:48:00,726 --> 00:48:01,927
when we first met was you, Do Gon.

1129
00:48:02,928 --> 00:48:06,498
Everyone else teased me all the time,

1130
00:48:06,498 --> 00:48:10,836
but you were the only one who didn't.

1131
00:48:12,171 --> 00:48:15,607
So to be completely honest,

1132
00:48:15,607 --> 00:48:16,909
I thought, "I'm curious about him."

1133
00:48:17,843 --> 00:48:19,211
You really piqued my interest.

1134
00:48:20,479 --> 00:48:21,446
So...

1135
00:48:22,281 --> 00:48:23,715
I decided to go on a date with you.

1136
00:48:26,285 --> 00:48:29,888
(Na Young reveals what first drew her in.)

1137
00:48:30,789 --> 00:48:33,959
(Two people alike yet different)

1138
00:48:33,959 --> 00:48:37,596
(Can they grow closer?)

1139
00:48:38,931 --> 00:48:40,032
Do you want to go get some meat?

1140
00:48:41,066 --> 00:48:42,901
(They move to their next destination.)

1141
00:48:42,901 --> 00:48:43,936
This is the place.

1142
00:48:45,237 --> 00:48:46,872
You can set your things down here.

1143
00:48:46,872 --> 00:48:47,706
I'm okay.

1144
00:48:47,706 --> 00:48:50,175
(Second stop, an outdoor barbecue spot)

1145
00:48:50,509 --> 00:48:52,344
(Sizzles)

1146
00:48:52,344 --> 00:48:54,112
When you think about dating,

1147
00:48:54,112 --> 00:48:57,049
what worries you the most?

1148
00:48:57,449 --> 00:48:59,284
Probably my health.

1149
00:49:00,419 --> 00:49:01,687
For example,

1150
00:49:02,221 --> 00:49:05,657
on the day of our date...

1151
00:49:05,657 --> 00:49:06,825
or just suddenly,

1152
00:49:06,825 --> 00:49:09,094
I start feeling unwell.

1153
00:49:10,429 --> 00:49:13,765
People can tell right away.

1154
00:49:13,765 --> 00:49:16,568
I feel bad when it happens.

1155
00:49:17,436 --> 00:49:19,238
A date might have to be cut short...

1156
00:49:19,238 --> 00:49:20,506
because of me.

1157
00:49:20,506 --> 00:49:21,673
We'd have no choice but to stop.

1158
00:49:22,307 --> 00:49:24,676
Sometimes I just collapse.

1159
00:49:24,676 --> 00:49:25,944
Completely out of nowhere.

1160
00:49:25,944 --> 00:49:27,212
Suddenly?

1161
00:49:27,212 --> 00:49:30,182
I can feel totally fine, then suddenly...

1162
00:49:30,549 --> 00:49:32,384
I head straight for the bathroom...

1163
00:49:32,384 --> 00:49:33,585
because I don't want to ruin it
for anyone.

1164
00:49:35,487 --> 00:49:36,722
So I always feel bad.

1165
00:49:36,722 --> 00:49:39,091
When that happens on a date...

1166
00:49:40,959 --> 00:49:42,861
You always feel guilty.

1167
00:49:42,861 --> 00:49:44,062
Yes, always.

1168
00:49:44,763 --> 00:49:45,831
Always.

1169
00:49:47,432 --> 00:49:50,235
(They relate to each other's stories...)

1170
00:49:50,235 --> 00:49:54,206
(and grow closer.)

1171
00:49:58,810 --> 00:50:02,548
I really wanted to know something.

1172
00:50:04,449 --> 00:50:05,717
Am I being too blunt?

1173
00:50:05,717 --> 00:50:08,220
I'm a pretty straightforward person.

1174
00:50:09,421 --> 00:50:11,256
Even from the start,

1175
00:50:11,256 --> 00:50:14,359
it was obvious who you were into.

1176
00:50:15,794 --> 00:50:20,098
Had you already decided on one person?

1177
00:50:20,098 --> 00:50:21,967
Or...

1178
00:50:21,967 --> 00:50:24,903
are you still open? I wanted to know that.

1179
00:50:24,903 --> 00:50:26,738
(Na Young wonders how Do Gon feels now.)

1180
00:50:27,873 --> 00:50:29,374
Honestly,

1181
00:50:29,374 --> 00:50:32,377
when someone makes me curious,

1182
00:50:33,979 --> 00:50:37,182
I want to talk to them.

1183
00:50:37,182 --> 00:50:39,952
So that's what I did.

1184
00:50:41,954 --> 00:50:43,889
But our conversations were so brief.

1185
00:50:44,957 --> 00:50:47,860
So when I got another date,

1186
00:50:47,860 --> 00:50:49,728
I wanted to see her somewhere else...

1187
00:50:49,728 --> 00:50:51,763
and talk some more.

1188
00:50:52,431 --> 00:50:54,433
That's why I chose her.

1189
00:50:56,902 --> 00:50:59,938
But I'm open. I barely know anyone yet.

1190
00:51:00,405 --> 00:51:01,573
(Nods)

1191
00:51:03,542 --> 00:51:05,444
So you're open to others?

1192
00:51:05,844 --> 00:51:06,745
Yeah.

1193
00:51:08,914 --> 00:51:10,782
Then can I flirt with you more openly?

1194
00:51:12,784 --> 00:51:14,686
(Laughs)

1195
00:51:15,687 --> 00:51:17,089
My gosh.

1196
00:51:17,089 --> 00:51:18,090
Hold on.

1197
00:51:18,090 --> 00:51:20,526
What do we do?

1198
00:51:20,526 --> 00:51:21,360
I'm rooting for them.

1199
00:51:21,360 --> 00:51:23,162
(Pleased)

1200
00:51:23,662 --> 00:51:25,030
I like this.

1201
00:51:25,030 --> 00:51:26,532
She's fearless.

1202
00:51:26,532 --> 00:51:27,466
She's charming.

1203
00:51:27,466 --> 00:51:28,800
She's so charming.

1204
00:51:28,800 --> 00:51:30,202
These two seem so well matched.

1205
00:51:32,905 --> 00:51:36,508
(Na Young declares her intent to flirt.)

1206
00:51:37,809 --> 00:51:39,444
I don't know how to do it.

1207
00:51:41,180 --> 00:51:42,548
I bet you're popular.

1208
00:51:45,350 --> 00:51:46,218
Not at all.

1209
00:51:47,853 --> 00:51:49,721
I can't exactly say I'm popular.

1210
00:51:49,721 --> 00:51:50,856
Why not? Own it.

1211
00:51:50,856 --> 00:51:52,925
You could say you got some attention.

1212
00:51:54,793 --> 00:51:55,961
You're really handsome.

1213
00:51:57,095 --> 00:51:59,631
(She begins flirting right away.)

1214
00:52:01,834 --> 00:52:03,969
You seem to know it too.

1215
00:52:04,603 --> 00:52:08,941
(Her honesty makes Do Gon smile.)

1216
00:52:09,541 --> 00:52:11,009
Yesterday,

1217
00:52:11,009 --> 00:52:14,279
you said you'd want to propose.

1218
00:52:20,452 --> 00:52:22,821
(Your date lasts for your combined time.)

1219
00:52:22,821 --> 00:52:26,258
(Han Do Gon and Kim Na Young,
your 100-minute date has ended.)

1220
00:52:28,460 --> 00:52:31,797
(Na Young, 100 min / Do Gon, 0 min)

1221
00:52:33,298 --> 00:52:34,633
They're out of time.

1222
00:52:34,633 --> 00:52:35,934
No.

1223
00:52:36,368 --> 00:52:38,737
Just when things were getting good.

1224
00:52:38,737 --> 00:52:40,606
- They were about to open up.
- So sweet.

1225
00:52:40,606 --> 00:52:41,840
It's too short.

1226
00:52:42,708 --> 00:52:44,443
They haven't even had the stew.

1227
00:52:44,443 --> 00:52:45,844
(Laughs)

1228
00:52:45,844 --> 00:52:48,013
- They can't end it now.
- That flew by.

1229
00:52:48,013 --> 00:52:49,548
It ended before they even ate.

1230
00:52:49,982 --> 00:52:51,583
Why did time fly so fast?

1231
00:52:51,583 --> 00:52:53,685
A hundred minutes sounds like a lot.

1232
00:52:53,685 --> 00:52:54,553
Exactly.

1233
00:52:54,553 --> 00:52:55,454
But it's short.

1234
00:52:55,454 --> 00:52:57,022
It isn't even two hours.

1235
00:52:57,022 --> 00:52:57,890
Seriously.

1236
00:52:58,390 --> 00:53:00,526
That timer is brutal.

1237
00:53:00,526 --> 00:53:01,426
Seriously.

1238
00:53:03,162 --> 00:53:05,531
(Na Young checks the text.)

1239
00:53:06,098 --> 00:53:07,466
Did you enjoy everything?

1240
00:53:07,466 --> 00:53:08,667
It was delicious.

1241
00:53:08,667 --> 00:53:09,701
It's so good.

1242
00:53:11,203 --> 00:53:12,704
You really planned quite a date.

1243
00:53:15,140 --> 00:53:16,175
Would you like some water?

1244
00:53:16,742 --> 00:53:18,243
Yes, thank you.

1245
00:53:19,011 --> 00:53:23,615
(Q. How did the text make you feel?)

1246
00:53:26,418 --> 00:53:28,453
I was the only one who chose him.

1247
00:53:28,453 --> 00:53:30,189
I knew that much for sure.

1248
00:53:31,023 --> 00:53:33,792
But that was before...

1249
00:53:33,792 --> 00:53:35,727
we'd even gone on the date.

1250
00:53:35,727 --> 00:53:37,930
So I thought it didn't matter.

1251
00:53:37,930 --> 00:53:42,067
When the date ended, I felt disappointed.

1252
00:53:42,067 --> 00:53:44,002
I wanted to talk more.

1253
00:53:44,770 --> 00:53:49,208
Maybe things will change after this date.

1254
00:53:49,208 --> 00:53:52,811
I felt like we'd gotten a little closer.

1255
00:53:53,779 --> 00:53:57,249
Of course, I knew how much time...

1256
00:53:57,249 --> 00:53:59,218
Na Young had given me...

1257
00:53:59,218 --> 00:54:03,322
because I'd spent my time on Ro Bin.

1258
00:54:03,322 --> 00:54:06,558
I felt a little guilty.

1259
00:54:07,493 --> 00:54:13,098
I wondered how to keep things going...

1260
00:54:13,098 --> 00:54:15,434
with Na Young from here.

1261
00:54:15,434 --> 00:54:17,803
It crossed my mind, however briefly.

1262
00:54:22,007 --> 00:54:23,509
I'll get going, then.

1263
00:54:23,509 --> 00:54:25,377
See you back at the House.

1264
00:54:25,377 --> 00:54:26,645
- Thanks for the meal.
- Sure.

1265
00:54:29,314 --> 00:54:32,251
(Different yet alike)

1266
00:54:32,251 --> 00:54:37,656
(Their time together ends.)

1267
00:54:41,994 --> 00:54:45,797
I love the Na-Gon pairing so much.

1268
00:54:45,797 --> 00:54:47,799
- Na Young and Do Gon.
- Me too.

1269
00:54:47,799 --> 00:54:49,101
They looked so good together.

1270
00:54:49,101 --> 00:54:50,769
So where does that leave Do Gon?

1271
00:54:52,104 --> 00:54:53,605
- That's the question.
- Exactly.

1272
00:54:53,605 --> 00:54:54,406
He got 100 minutes...

1273
00:54:54,406 --> 00:54:57,609
and gave 100 minutes to someone else.

1274
00:54:57,609 --> 00:54:59,645
He gave Ro Bin...

1275
00:54:59,645 --> 00:55:01,747
one hundred minutes over two choices.

1276
00:55:02,080 --> 00:55:02,915
That's impressive.

1277
00:55:02,915 --> 00:55:04,550
Let's watch Do Gon's face.

1278
00:55:04,550 --> 00:55:06,318
I can't wait to see his reaction.

1279
00:55:09,688 --> 00:55:10,622
Did you wait long?

1280
00:55:10,622 --> 00:55:12,024
No, not very long.

1281
00:55:12,457 --> 00:55:13,992
I just got here myself.

1282
00:55:13,992 --> 00:55:15,394
- Really?
- Yes.

1283
00:55:15,394 --> 00:55:16,762
Up on the second floor.

1284
00:55:16,762 --> 00:55:19,097
(Do Gon and Ro Bin's second date begins.)

1285
00:55:19,565 --> 00:55:22,234
I've wanted to check this place out.

1286
00:55:22,234 --> 00:55:23,569
Do you know it?

1287
00:55:23,569 --> 00:55:25,637
I've heard of it but never been.

1288
00:55:25,637 --> 00:55:27,039
You've heard of it but never been?

1289
00:55:27,039 --> 00:55:28,574
Same here.

1290
00:55:28,574 --> 00:55:30,909
- Perfect.
- Is this it? Really?

1291
00:55:30,909 --> 00:55:35,581
It's known for its healthy bread.

1292
00:55:37,216 --> 00:55:38,617
Hello. Let's sit there.

1293
00:55:39,785 --> 00:55:40,919
Hello.

1294
00:55:44,256 --> 00:55:45,457
- So this is the place.
- Cool.

1295
00:55:46,625 --> 00:55:50,662
(After two dates,
have their feelings changed?)

1296
00:55:52,598 --> 00:55:53,699
It's cold out, isn't it?

1297
00:55:53,699 --> 00:55:54,800
It is.

1298
00:55:54,800 --> 00:55:56,568
I should've brought a jacket.

1299
00:55:57,469 --> 00:55:59,338
- Is that all you're wearing?
- Yes.

1300
00:55:59,338 --> 00:56:01,773
This is still my warmest outfit...

1301
00:56:01,773 --> 00:56:03,008
out of everything I brought.

1302
00:56:03,008 --> 00:56:05,077
So you didn't bring a coat.

1303
00:56:05,077 --> 00:56:08,547
I did, but it didn't go with this outfit.

1304
00:56:08,547 --> 00:56:09,748
Too bad.

1305
00:56:09,748 --> 00:56:11,450
I brought extras. Ask if you need one.

1306
00:56:11,450 --> 00:56:12,351
Really?

1307
00:56:12,351 --> 00:56:13,919
- Just in case.
- Great.

1308
00:56:14,353 --> 00:56:19,158
I wondered how much time Ro Bin gave me.

1309
00:56:19,158 --> 00:56:21,593
On our date,

1310
00:56:21,593 --> 00:56:24,296
I wanted to see...

1311
00:56:24,296 --> 00:56:25,464
if her feelings for me had changed.

1312
00:56:26,798 --> 00:56:30,369
(Do Gon wonders how Ro Bin feels.)

1313
00:56:35,507 --> 00:56:37,476
Did you think we'd date again today?

1314
00:56:39,912 --> 00:56:41,079
(Flustered)

1315
00:56:41,747 --> 00:56:44,149
Me? I had no idea.

1316
00:56:44,149 --> 00:56:45,484
- You didn't?
- No.

1317
00:56:46,285 --> 00:56:47,419
Why?

1318
00:56:47,419 --> 00:56:48,620
I...

1319
00:56:49,421 --> 00:56:50,622
(Curious)

1320
00:56:51,223 --> 00:56:52,825
I don't know. I just didn't expect it.

1321
00:56:54,760 --> 00:56:55,928
I really didn't.

1322
00:56:55,928 --> 00:56:56,829
Not at all?

1323
00:56:58,063 --> 00:57:01,366
I wouldn't say not at all.

1324
00:57:01,366 --> 00:57:03,502
I figured it could go either way.

1325
00:57:03,502 --> 00:57:05,470
That's just the sense I got.

1326
00:57:06,138 --> 00:57:08,173
Because yesterday was so much fun.

1327
00:57:09,041 --> 00:57:10,042
Did you have fun yesterday?

1328
00:57:10,342 --> 00:57:12,044
Yes, I did.

1329
00:57:14,980 --> 00:57:16,448
How many people are you interested in?

1330
00:57:16,448 --> 00:57:17,282
Me?

1331
00:57:18,617 --> 00:57:19,585
I...

1332
00:57:20,986 --> 00:57:21,920
Why?

1333
00:57:23,640 --> 00:57:24,608
Hundred Do Gon.

1334
00:57:24,608 --> 00:57:26,677
He's acting so different now, isn't he?

1335
00:57:27,377 --> 00:57:29,112
It's day three, and little by little,

1336
00:57:29,112 --> 00:57:31,114
everyone's getting more proactive.

1337
00:57:31,114 --> 00:57:31,915
They're asking questions.

1338
00:57:31,915 --> 00:57:33,050
Exactly.

1339
00:57:33,050 --> 00:57:33,717
(Focused)

1340
00:57:34,384 --> 00:57:36,386
- People I'm interested in?
- Yes.

1341
00:57:36,386 --> 00:57:38,889
For now, there are...

1342
00:57:39,957 --> 00:57:40,757
two.

1343
00:57:40,757 --> 00:57:41,625
Two.

1344
00:57:42,626 --> 00:57:43,460
Two.

1345
00:57:43,827 --> 00:57:47,297
(Ro Bin says there are two.)

1346
00:57:48,265 --> 00:57:51,668
One is someone I'm just curious about.

1347
00:57:51,668 --> 00:57:53,337
I'm curious and interested in him.

1348
00:57:55,405 --> 00:57:56,406
And you're interested in the other one?

1349
00:57:57,074 --> 00:57:59,409
The other, I'm still not sure about.

1350
00:57:59,409 --> 00:58:02,045
I think I need to talk to him more.

1351
00:58:04,882 --> 00:58:05,849
I'm curious who they are.

1352
00:58:08,585 --> 00:58:10,487
I think that's about it.

1353
00:58:11,088 --> 00:58:12,156
(Sneaks a glance)

1354
00:58:13,190 --> 00:58:14,158
Can I ask you too?

1355
00:58:15,893 --> 00:58:17,728
As for me,

1356
00:58:17,728 --> 00:58:20,097
there's one person I'm interested in.

1357
00:58:24,034 --> 00:58:26,970
(Do Gon answers without hesitation.)

1358
00:58:26,970 --> 00:58:28,972
As expected, Do Gon is different.

1359
00:58:28,972 --> 00:58:31,608
- He's being completely honest.
- He is.

1360
00:58:31,608 --> 00:58:33,110
He's practically...

1361
00:58:33,110 --> 00:58:35,812
- telling her outright.
- Right.

1362
00:58:37,781 --> 00:58:39,183
I'm not closed off,

1363
00:58:40,450 --> 00:58:43,120
but I think it'd be better...

1364
00:58:43,120 --> 00:58:44,955
to spend more time talking...

1365
00:58:44,955 --> 00:58:46,957
to the person I'm curious about.

1366
00:58:48,592 --> 00:58:51,461
(Their juice arrives.)

1367
00:58:51,461 --> 00:58:52,896
Let's try each other's drinks.

1368
00:58:53,697 --> 00:58:54,865
(Slides off the wrapper)

1369
00:58:56,567 --> 00:58:57,601
(Takes it)

1370
00:58:58,402 --> 00:59:02,039
(Do Gon tidies up Ro Bin's things too.)

1371
00:59:04,474 --> 00:59:06,109
This is so good. Do you want to try it?

1372
00:59:06,777 --> 00:59:08,879
I'll try with my straw.
I haven't touched it yet.

1373
00:59:08,879 --> 00:59:10,214
Right. Drink from that side.

1374
00:59:11,915 --> 00:59:12,916
It's good, right?

1375
00:59:12,916 --> 00:59:16,053
It tastes like real grape juice.

1376
00:59:16,053 --> 00:59:17,988
Exactly.

1377
00:59:17,988 --> 00:59:18,889
It's good.

1378
00:59:22,593 --> 00:59:23,460
Yesterday,

1379
00:59:23,460 --> 00:59:26,096
I gave you a lot of my time.

1380
00:59:26,096 --> 00:59:27,965
You found out after it ended.

1381
00:59:28,465 --> 00:59:31,335
Did anything change after that?

1382
00:59:31,335 --> 00:59:33,437
A change?

1383
00:59:34,505 --> 00:59:36,573
In any way at all?

1384
00:59:36,573 --> 00:59:38,308
(Nods)

1385
00:59:39,843 --> 00:59:42,279
Something did change.

1386
00:59:43,380 --> 00:59:46,150
As we talked,

1387
00:59:47,117 --> 00:59:50,454
I felt like there might be an age gap.

1388
00:59:50,454 --> 00:59:52,523
Really? You picked up on that?

1389
00:59:52,523 --> 00:59:55,492
I could be wrong,

1390
00:59:57,628 --> 01:00:00,697
but I started feeling intimidated,

1391
01:00:00,697 --> 01:00:02,366
and I guess I also...

1392
01:00:02,366 --> 01:00:05,969
saw you as such a mature adult...

1393
01:00:05,969 --> 01:00:08,005
that without realizing it,

1394
01:00:08,005 --> 01:00:10,974
I felt like I was acting grown-up...

1395
01:00:10,974 --> 01:00:12,209
and trying to match your energy.

1396
01:00:12,209 --> 01:00:13,277
Yesterday?

1397
01:00:13,277 --> 01:00:15,145
Really?

1398
01:00:18,115 --> 01:00:23,387
(Ro Bin shares how the date felt.)

1399
01:00:23,987 --> 01:00:26,323
When we talked yesterday...

1400
01:00:26,323 --> 01:00:28,759
back at the house with everyone,

1401
01:00:28,759 --> 01:00:31,261
we talked about dating older or younger.

1402
01:00:31,261 --> 01:00:33,230
Right, we did.

1403
01:00:33,230 --> 01:00:36,233
I think you said you wanted...

1404
01:00:36,233 --> 01:00:37,968
a comfortable, friend-like relationship...

1405
01:00:37,968 --> 01:00:40,170
with someone your age or younger.

1406
01:00:40,170 --> 01:00:43,807
Older is fine if the age gap feels small.

1407
01:00:44,174 --> 01:00:45,442
(Nods)

1408
01:00:46,143 --> 01:00:48,178
Up to four years would be okay.

1409
01:00:48,178 --> 01:00:49,146
Four years.

1410
01:00:51,014 --> 01:00:51,949
Why?

1411
01:00:53,183 --> 01:00:54,017
(Hurt)

1412
01:00:54,017 --> 01:00:54,785
Wait.

1413
01:00:54,785 --> 01:00:57,254
(I can't watch.)

1414
01:00:57,788 --> 01:00:59,223
(That hurt.)

1415
01:00:59,223 --> 01:01:01,458
She said she could feel the age gap,

1416
01:01:01,458 --> 01:01:03,193
- then said she wants...
- Someone her age.

1417
01:01:03,193 --> 01:01:05,195
to date someone her own age.

1418
01:01:05,195 --> 01:01:07,664
I bet when they get back,

1419
01:01:07,664 --> 01:01:09,666
Ro Bin will apologize again.

1420
01:01:09,666 --> 01:01:11,201
At night?

1421
01:01:11,201 --> 01:01:14,404
"What I said earlier..."

1422
01:01:14,404 --> 01:01:17,341
She's incredibly honest.

1423
01:01:17,341 --> 01:01:19,610
She does say things very directly.

1424
01:01:19,610 --> 01:01:21,345
(Feeling bad for him)

1425
01:01:21,345 --> 01:01:23,614
Do Gon is starting to get the message.

1426
01:01:25,315 --> 01:01:26,250
Why?

1427
01:01:26,884 --> 01:01:28,218
I'm curious about something.

1428
01:01:28,218 --> 01:01:30,921
You said younger would be okay, right?

1429
01:01:30,921 --> 01:01:34,057
How much younger would you date?

1430
01:01:34,057 --> 01:01:34,992
Younger?

1431
01:01:37,094 --> 01:01:38,028
Younger...

1432
01:01:39,429 --> 01:01:41,532
(Stares)

1433
01:01:42,332 --> 01:01:45,135
Just as someone could be older,

1434
01:01:46,136 --> 01:01:48,839
if they're working, age matters less.

1435
01:01:50,774 --> 01:01:52,843
If they had a job?

1436
01:01:52,843 --> 01:01:55,913
- Rather than being a student.
- Right.

1437
01:01:56,680 --> 01:01:57,915
What if they were a student?

1438
01:01:58,375 --> 01:01:59,349
If they were a student,

1439
01:02:03,220 --> 01:02:05,088
- I don't think I could.
- Really?

1440
01:02:05,088 --> 01:02:07,157
For their sake.

1441
01:02:08,759 --> 01:02:10,561
I see.

1442
01:02:10,561 --> 01:02:12,596
I could end up looking like a jerk.

1443
01:02:12,596 --> 01:02:14,298
I know exactly what you mean.

1444
01:02:15,566 --> 01:02:17,601
(Spicy rice cakes end the age debate.)

1445
01:02:17,601 --> 01:02:19,002
- I haven't had this in forever.
- Me neither.

1446
01:02:19,002 --> 01:02:19,970
Do you like it?

1447
01:02:19,970 --> 01:02:21,271
I do, but I rarely eat it.

1448
01:02:22,105 --> 01:02:23,273
Thank you.

1449
01:02:25,976 --> 01:02:30,147
(As always, Do Gon serves Ro Bin first.)

1450
01:02:31,348 --> 01:02:32,916
It's really hot.

1451
01:02:32,916 --> 01:02:34,218
It is.

1452
01:02:34,218 --> 01:02:35,752
(Blows)

1453
01:02:36,186 --> 01:02:37,254
(Bite)

1454
01:02:42,726 --> 01:02:43,760
It's spicy.

1455
01:02:46,096 --> 01:02:47,564
Can I ask you something?

1456
01:02:47,564 --> 01:02:50,067
Do I seem like a student or like I work?

1457
01:02:51,034 --> 01:02:52,369
(Curious)

1458
01:02:53,170 --> 01:02:54,037
(Thinks)

1459
01:02:54,037 --> 01:02:55,105
You're not sure?

1460
01:02:55,105 --> 01:02:56,073
You look like you have a job.

1461
01:02:56,073 --> 01:02:57,174
Like I have a job?

1462
01:03:05,716 --> 01:03:06,950
I want to find out soon.

1463
01:03:08,552 --> 01:03:12,256
I'm curious about everyone's job and age.

1464
01:03:12,256 --> 01:03:14,224
Don't you think we'll find out today?

1465
01:03:14,224 --> 01:03:15,859
Yeah, I have a feeling.

1466
01:03:15,859 --> 01:03:16,627
Right?

1467
01:03:17,427 --> 01:03:20,197
I'm so curious about what you do, Do Gon.

1468
01:03:20,197 --> 01:03:21,498
My age?

1469
01:03:21,498 --> 01:03:22,533
What I do for work?

1470
01:03:22,533 --> 01:03:24,101
I'm curious about your age too.

1471
01:03:24,101 --> 01:03:25,702
I really want to know both.

1472
01:03:26,837 --> 01:03:29,206
I hope our age gap is under five years.

1473
01:03:37,181 --> 01:03:40,384
Are there any other dates
you'd like to try here?

1474
01:03:40,384 --> 01:03:41,819
Another date I'd like to try?

1475
01:03:42,786 --> 01:03:44,221
The restaurant I want to visit...

1476
01:03:44,221 --> 01:03:45,722
You read my bucket list, didn't you?

1477
01:03:46,790 --> 01:03:47,991
- You got it, right?
- Yes.

1478
01:03:49,593 --> 01:03:51,295
Anything else besides those?

1479
01:03:51,295 --> 01:03:52,529
You mean anything else?

1480
01:03:52,529 --> 01:03:53,530
Well...

1481
01:03:54,164 --> 01:03:55,299
I...

1482
01:03:55,799 --> 01:03:58,168
I like table tennis,

1483
01:03:59,536 --> 01:04:02,539
so maybe we could play sometime?

1484
01:04:02,539 --> 01:04:03,740
Do you play table tennis?

1485
01:04:03,740 --> 01:04:05,042
I sure do.

1486
01:04:05,042 --> 01:04:06,076
Really?

1487
01:04:06,076 --> 01:04:07,544
Table tennis, tennis, things like that.

1488
01:04:07,544 --> 01:04:08,812
Seriously?

1489
01:04:09,379 --> 01:04:10,547
I had no idea...

1490
01:04:12,115 --> 01:04:14,485
you could play table tennis and tennis.

1491
01:04:14,485 --> 01:04:16,086
You said you hardly ever exercised...

1492
01:04:16,086 --> 01:04:17,921
or did anything athletic.

1493
01:04:17,921 --> 01:04:18,922
No, I didn't.

1494
01:04:18,922 --> 01:04:20,257
- Did you say you work out?
- I did.

1495
01:04:20,257 --> 01:04:21,058
You did?

1496
01:04:21,058 --> 01:04:22,726
- I said I like active sports.
- Light...

1497
01:04:22,726 --> 01:04:23,827
Did you?

1498
01:04:24,194 --> 01:04:26,330
- Aren't you confusing me with someone?
- Sorry.

1499
01:04:26,563 --> 01:04:28,465
(Hurt)

1500
01:04:29,766 --> 01:04:31,268
I see.

1501
01:04:33,270 --> 01:04:35,739
She mixed him up with Jong Eun.

1502
01:04:35,739 --> 01:04:36,707
I'm losing it.

1503
01:04:37,474 --> 01:04:38,509
Ro Bin...

1504
01:04:38,509 --> 01:04:41,044
went on a date with Jong Eun...

1505
01:04:41,044 --> 01:04:44,481
and got her big dopamine hit there.

1506
01:04:44,481 --> 01:04:47,651
That rush is affecting this date now.

1507
01:04:48,218 --> 01:04:49,520
That hurts.

1508
01:04:49,520 --> 01:04:50,687
It hurts.

1509
01:04:51,288 --> 01:04:53,157
A fool who only thinks of you.

1510
01:04:53,690 --> 01:04:54,691
He only has eyes for you.

1511
01:04:54,691 --> 01:04:56,193
A fool who only sees you.

1512
01:04:56,193 --> 01:04:57,094
(Upset)

1513
01:04:57,528 --> 01:04:58,795
That's so upsetting.

1514
01:05:03,033 --> 01:05:05,235
Do you have something else scheduled?

1515
01:05:05,235 --> 01:05:06,537
After this?

1516
01:05:07,204 --> 01:05:08,338
Do you think I do?

1517
01:05:10,807 --> 01:05:12,543
I think you were busy before this date.

1518
01:05:13,744 --> 01:05:15,012
(Flustered)

1519
01:05:15,445 --> 01:05:17,247
You'll probably head back to the House.

1520
01:05:18,148 --> 01:05:19,950
Are you good at picking up on things?

1521
01:05:21,018 --> 01:05:22,820
A little.

1522
01:05:24,288 --> 01:05:26,723
Even when we parted earlier,

1523
01:05:26,723 --> 01:05:28,692
I knew you were going on another date.

1524
01:05:29,426 --> 01:05:30,394
(Sorry)

1525
01:05:31,328 --> 01:05:32,596
Was it that obvious?

1526
01:05:33,096 --> 01:05:35,866
No, I just figured.

1527
01:05:40,237 --> 01:05:42,472
(The date lasts for your combined time.)

1528
01:05:42,472 --> 01:05:48,312
(Seo Ro Bin and Han Do Gon,
your 100-minute date has ended.)

1529
01:05:50,547 --> 01:05:53,851
(Do Gon, 100 minutes / Ro Bin, 0 minutes)

1530
01:05:56,487 --> 01:06:02,726
(A difference in feelings they can't hide)

1531
01:06:03,494 --> 01:06:04,428
Okay.

1532
01:06:04,761 --> 01:06:09,399
I got the text saying our 100 minutes...

1533
01:06:09,933 --> 01:06:11,768
had run out.

1534
01:06:11,768 --> 01:06:14,938
I realized Ro Bin...

1535
01:06:14,938 --> 01:06:16,773
probably wasn't that interested in me.

1536
01:06:16,773 --> 01:06:18,175
It gave me a lot to think about.

1537
01:06:18,175 --> 01:06:20,310
Should I keep trying?

1538
01:06:21,078 --> 01:06:24,515
It definitely made me more cautious.

1539
01:06:25,415 --> 01:06:27,017
(Sorry)

1540
01:06:29,319 --> 01:06:31,822
Do you want to take a few pictures?

1541
01:06:33,056 --> 01:06:34,491
Black-and-white...

1542
01:06:34,491 --> 01:06:36,226
(He changes the subject.)

1543
01:06:36,226 --> 01:06:38,128
Black-and-white has a different feel,

1544
01:06:38,795 --> 01:06:40,597
so I brought two cameras on purpose.

1545
01:06:40,597 --> 01:06:42,466
One for black-and-white, one for color.

1546
01:06:42,466 --> 01:06:44,434
- Let's use both.
- Let's take the same shot.

1547
01:06:44,434 --> 01:06:45,769
The same shot? That sounds good.

1548
01:06:46,470 --> 01:06:47,871
Are you taking my picture?

1549
01:06:47,871 --> 01:06:48,639
Yes.

1550
01:06:48,639 --> 01:06:49,540
Okay.

1551
01:06:52,142 --> 01:06:54,678
I don't know how they'll turn out,

1552
01:06:56,113 --> 01:06:57,514
but I'll send them when they're developed.

1553
01:06:57,514 --> 01:06:58,916
You'll send them to me?

1554
01:07:01,018 --> 01:07:01,985
One, two, three.

1555
01:07:03,620 --> 01:07:06,757
(Will their roll of film...)

1556
01:07:06,757 --> 01:07:11,895
(hold even more memories?)

1557
01:07:19,937 --> 01:07:21,538
(Meanwhile, at the House)

1558
01:07:22,306 --> 01:07:24,107
(Na Young returns from seeing Do Gon.)

1559
01:07:24,107 --> 01:07:25,209
Goodness.

1560
01:07:28,512 --> 01:07:31,148
(Ryun Gi was in the House alone.)

1561
01:07:31,515 --> 01:07:32,583
Who is it?

1562
01:07:34,952 --> 01:07:35,953
Who are you?

1563
01:07:38,522 --> 01:07:39,523
Who are you?

1564
01:07:39,523 --> 01:07:41,158
I asked you first.

1565
01:07:42,292 --> 01:07:43,961
You're back.

1566
01:07:44,261 --> 01:07:45,329
When did you get here?

1567
01:07:45,329 --> 01:07:47,464
I've been here the whole time.

1568
01:07:47,464 --> 01:07:48,499
Did you just get back?

1569
01:07:48,499 --> 01:07:49,399
Yes.

1570
01:07:50,334 --> 01:07:51,568
What are you doing?

1571
01:07:51,568 --> 01:07:56,240
I just woke up from a nap here.

1572
01:07:56,240 --> 01:07:57,508
Would you like to chat?

1573
01:07:57,508 --> 01:07:58,208
Sure.

1574
01:07:58,208 --> 01:07:59,510
Do you want to chat for a bit?

1575
01:08:01,378 --> 01:08:04,615
(Their first conversation alone.)

1576
01:08:04,615 --> 01:08:05,782
After you.

1577
01:08:05,782 --> 01:08:06,750
Thanks.

1578
01:08:07,518 --> 01:08:09,753
The air feels pretty nice.

1579
01:08:09,753 --> 01:08:11,421
It does. It's so nice.

1580
01:08:12,456 --> 01:08:14,424
How would you describe your personality?

1581
01:08:14,424 --> 01:08:15,559
I...

1582
01:08:16,059 --> 01:08:18,295
don't usually tell people these things.

1583
01:08:18,295 --> 01:08:21,365
My weaknesses, insecurities, struggles.

1584
01:08:21,365 --> 01:08:23,000
I don't like letting them show.

1585
01:08:23,000 --> 01:08:25,802
I think I'm still...

1586
01:08:26,770 --> 01:08:28,038
not very good at that.

1587
01:08:29,206 --> 01:08:30,841
Before I came here,

1588
01:08:30,841 --> 01:08:33,610
that was my biggest concern.

1589
01:08:33,610 --> 01:08:35,546
I'm not fully recovered,

1590
01:08:35,546 --> 01:08:38,048
and it's hard to meet someone...

1591
01:08:38,916 --> 01:08:41,218
when I don't have the headspace for it.

1592
01:08:42,619 --> 01:08:44,021
I feel guilty too.

1593
01:08:44,021 --> 01:08:45,489
Even now?

1594
01:08:46,123 --> 01:08:48,192
Anyone dating me...

1595
01:08:49,193 --> 01:08:52,896
might have more fun with someone healthy.

1596
01:08:52,896 --> 01:08:54,665
It's natural to think that.

1597
01:08:54,665 --> 01:08:55,866
They'd have a happy relationship.

1598
01:08:55,866 --> 01:08:58,001
So why choose me? That's where it starts.

1599
01:08:58,669 --> 01:09:01,705
Stomach cancer comes with unique issues.

1600
01:09:02,105 --> 01:09:04,208
Even ordinary things couples do...

1601
01:09:04,208 --> 01:09:06,343
like going out to eat...

1602
01:09:07,177 --> 01:09:08,545
can be difficult.

1603
01:09:09,279 --> 01:09:12,416
My stamina and drinking matter too.

1604
01:09:12,416 --> 01:09:16,119
I wouldn't drink much on a date,

1605
01:09:16,119 --> 01:09:19,656
but a drink can be part of the mood.

1606
01:09:20,657 --> 01:09:25,362
I came here carrying all those worries.

1607
01:09:25,963 --> 01:09:27,764
They're still with me,

1608
01:09:29,299 --> 01:09:32,102
and I keep having to face them.

1609
01:09:34,238 --> 01:09:37,040
Up until yesterday,

1610
01:09:37,040 --> 01:09:41,345
I couldn't shake those worries.

1611
01:09:42,045 --> 01:09:45,349
If anything, they kept coming back,

1612
01:09:45,349 --> 01:09:48,252
so I dwelled on them a lot.

1613
01:09:49,553 --> 01:09:52,422
After going out yesterday,

1614
01:09:52,422 --> 01:09:54,424
they hit me all over again.

1615
01:09:54,424 --> 01:09:55,826
Really? It got worse?

1616
01:09:55,826 --> 01:09:56,760
If anything, it did.

1617
01:09:58,328 --> 01:10:01,732
(Ryun Gi opens up about his worries.)

1618
01:10:02,266 --> 01:10:04,735
Honestly, it's...

1619
01:10:04,735 --> 01:10:05,669
How should I put this?

1620
01:10:06,703 --> 01:10:07,871
I completely understand.

1621
01:10:09,573 --> 01:10:11,942
If I hadn't been through it myself,

1622
01:10:11,942 --> 01:10:14,211
I think it would've been hard too.

1623
01:10:14,945 --> 01:10:17,881
But people may be more accepting,

1624
01:10:18,348 --> 01:10:21,185
and we're just worrying too far ahead.

1625
01:10:21,185 --> 01:10:22,653
Exactly.

1626
01:10:22,653 --> 01:10:25,422
The other person may not think that way.

1627
01:10:25,989 --> 01:10:29,393
They may feel hurt if we act like that.

1628
01:10:29,393 --> 01:10:30,961
Some people take it in stride.

1629
01:10:30,961 --> 01:10:32,329
They really do.

1630
01:10:32,329 --> 01:10:36,700
Why worry before anything even happens?

1631
01:10:36,700 --> 01:10:38,569
I heard that all the time.

1632
01:10:38,569 --> 01:10:41,371
I'd let my imagination run wild...

1633
01:10:41,371 --> 01:10:43,173
and ask, "What if that happens?"

1634
01:10:43,173 --> 01:10:45,576
I kept saying things like that.

1635
01:10:46,877 --> 01:10:49,313
They'd go, "Come on."

1636
01:10:49,313 --> 01:10:50,948
"Your body's struggling as it is."

1637
01:10:50,948 --> 01:10:52,950
"Why make things harder on yourself?"

1638
01:10:52,950 --> 01:10:57,321
After hearing that so many times,

1639
01:10:57,688 --> 01:11:01,391
I realized I'd gotten too far ahead...

1640
01:11:01,391 --> 01:11:05,262
and had only been tormenting myself.

1641
01:11:06,597 --> 01:11:11,602
(Two kindred souls comfort each other.)

1642
01:11:12,336 --> 01:11:14,571
(Meanwhile)

1643
01:11:18,141 --> 01:11:19,076
This is it.

1644
01:11:19,076 --> 01:11:20,577
(Seon Ho and Ye Ji's second date begins.)

1645
01:11:20,577 --> 01:11:22,479
This is it? It's so pretty.

1646
01:11:22,713 --> 01:11:23,580
Yes.

1647
01:11:25,048 --> 01:11:26,884
(Smiles)

1648
01:11:27,751 --> 01:11:29,286
All right, Ye Ji.

1649
01:11:30,053 --> 01:11:32,356
Don't change the channel, everyone.

1650
01:11:32,356 --> 01:11:33,957
Let's go, Ye Ji and Seon Ho.

1651
01:11:34,324 --> 01:11:35,726
Ye Ji and Seon Ho.

1652
01:11:35,726 --> 01:11:37,828
This couple.

1653
01:11:37,828 --> 01:11:38,996
I've been waiting for them.

1654
01:11:38,996 --> 01:11:40,631
Ye Ji can't stop smiling.

1655
01:11:40,631 --> 01:11:42,399
Fifty minutes each. It's even.

1656
01:11:42,399 --> 01:11:43,634
Show us what you've got today.

1657
01:11:43,634 --> 01:11:45,536
- Let's see how today goes.
- I'm curious.

1658
01:11:45,536 --> 01:11:47,504
(Heart pounding)

1659
01:11:47,971 --> 01:11:49,173
Let's go in.

1660
01:11:50,107 --> 01:11:51,141
Thank you.

1661
01:11:53,644 --> 01:11:56,346
- Hello.
- Hello.

1662
01:11:57,981 --> 01:12:01,318
(Ye Ji's bucket list,
having sweet strawberry cake)

1663
01:12:01,318 --> 01:12:04,721
I thought it'd be nice to share...

1664
01:12:04,721 --> 01:12:08,525
the food I craved most during treatment.

1665
01:12:08,525 --> 01:12:13,230
So I wrote "Having strawberry cake"
and gave it to Seon Ho.

1666
01:12:13,697 --> 01:12:14,865
Do you like strawberry cake?

1667
01:12:14,865 --> 01:12:15,899
Yes, I do.

1668
01:12:16,333 --> 01:12:17,367
Then,

1669
01:12:17,701 --> 01:12:21,104
can we eat some here and box the rest?

1670
01:12:21,104 --> 01:12:22,739
- Yes, that's fine.
- Should we do that, then?

1671
01:12:24,775 --> 01:12:25,809
I'm excited.

1672
01:12:27,845 --> 01:12:30,180
- It looks so good.
- It does.

1673
01:12:33,250 --> 01:12:34,785
You got my bucket list card, right?

1674
01:12:38,722 --> 01:12:40,357
(Shy)

1675
01:12:40,591 --> 01:12:42,059
Yes, I think I got it.

1676
01:12:42,860 --> 01:12:44,328
(Embarrassed)

1677
01:12:47,598 --> 01:12:48,999
Well...

1678
01:12:48,999 --> 01:12:50,367
Wasn't it cute?

1679
01:12:50,367 --> 01:12:52,336
Yes, it was really cute.

1680
01:12:53,136 --> 01:12:55,606
I liked the smiley face you drew.

1681
01:12:56,573 --> 01:12:58,375
Was cake what you wanted most?

1682
01:12:58,375 --> 01:13:01,211
Definitely strawberry cake.

1683
01:13:01,211 --> 01:13:02,346
Because...

1684
01:13:03,113 --> 01:13:05,349
during chemo, you can't eat fruit.

1685
01:13:05,349 --> 01:13:06,350
Right.

1686
01:13:06,350 --> 01:13:08,185
You can't have cake or whipped cream.

1687
01:13:08,185 --> 01:13:09,920
Whipped cream is especially bad.

1688
01:13:09,920 --> 01:13:13,157
On day 100 after my transplant...

1689
01:13:13,891 --> 01:13:16,894
or at Christmas, we'd get a cake,

1690
01:13:16,894 --> 01:13:18,695
but I was the only one who couldn't eat.

1691
01:13:19,563 --> 01:13:21,932
I never got over missing out on it.

1692
01:13:24,234 --> 01:13:25,536
This is what it looks like.

1693
01:13:26,503 --> 01:13:27,704
It's so pretty.

1694
01:13:29,006 --> 01:13:31,542
(Ye Ji's strawberry cake is ready.)

1695
01:13:31,542 --> 01:13:33,310
Thank you.

1696
01:13:33,310 --> 01:13:35,245
I should take a picture.

1697
01:13:35,245 --> 01:13:37,314
I don't think that strawberry is real.

1698
01:13:38,482 --> 01:13:39,449
This one?

1699
01:13:39,449 --> 01:13:40,484
Yeah, I see it now.

1700
01:13:40,784 --> 01:13:42,352
It's so well made.

1701
01:13:42,352 --> 01:13:44,087
- Right?
- You can't tell at a glance.

1702
01:13:47,157 --> 01:13:47,958
(Click)

1703
01:13:52,563 --> 01:13:53,864
Thank you.

1704
01:13:53,864 --> 01:13:56,033
(Strawberry cake secured)

1705
01:13:59,136 --> 01:14:04,241
(Their date begins after the pickup.)

1706
01:14:05,876 --> 01:14:07,311
This must be the place.

1707
01:14:07,311 --> 01:14:10,480
(She brings Seon Ho to another spot.)

1708
01:14:11,114 --> 01:14:13,183
(A warm, welcoming atmosphere)

1709
01:14:14,418 --> 01:14:15,486
(An old-school eatery)

1710
01:14:15,486 --> 01:14:16,453
This place is great.

1711
01:14:17,287 --> 01:14:18,489
This is the real deal.

1712
01:14:28,398 --> 01:14:29,199
Hello.

1713
01:14:29,199 --> 01:14:30,100
Two, please.

1714
01:14:31,401 --> 01:14:32,870
(Excited)

1715
01:14:34,004 --> 01:14:35,772
Sitting there...

1716
01:14:35,772 --> 01:14:37,207
and talking over a drink...

1717
01:14:37,207 --> 01:14:38,475
could bring them closer.

1718
01:14:38,475 --> 01:14:40,043
- Absolutely.
- It could change the mood.

1719
01:14:40,043 --> 01:14:41,612
A little alcohol might...

1720
01:14:41,612 --> 01:14:42,746
But you never know, everyone.

1721
01:14:44,314 --> 01:14:45,849
We have to watch until the end.

1722
01:14:45,849 --> 01:14:47,217
- We have to.
- You never know with Seon Ho.

1723
01:14:47,217 --> 01:14:48,152
I'm nervous.

1724
01:14:49,920 --> 01:14:51,755
There isn't a kettle, though.

1725
01:14:53,624 --> 01:14:55,425
- I'll pour you a glass.
- Okay.

1726
01:14:55,692 --> 01:14:57,394
(Pours)

1727
01:14:59,129 --> 01:15:00,097
Here you go.

1728
01:15:01,398 --> 01:15:04,101
(He pours Ye Ji her first drink.)

1729
01:15:04,601 --> 01:15:05,536
I'll pour yours.

1730
01:15:05,536 --> 01:15:06,470
Thank you.

1731
01:15:07,938 --> 01:15:09,306
(Smiles)

1732
01:15:09,306 --> 01:15:11,108
I can't believe we're drinking rice wine.

1733
01:15:15,179 --> 01:15:16,647
- Shall we have a drink?
- Sure.

1734
01:15:16,980 --> 01:15:18,215
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

1735
01:15:25,022 --> 01:15:26,190
This is delicious.

1736
01:15:26,190 --> 01:15:27,291
It's pretty good.

1737
01:15:29,359 --> 01:15:31,528
(Will their feelings deepen today?)

1738
01:15:31,528 --> 01:15:32,896
Thank you.

1739
01:15:33,230 --> 01:15:34,598
Yes, I'll take it.

1740
01:15:34,598 --> 01:15:35,666
It smells delicious.

1741
01:15:37,267 --> 01:15:40,170
(Spicy chicken feet are ready too.)

1742
01:15:40,170 --> 01:15:41,138
Thank you.

1743
01:15:41,138 --> 01:15:42,306
Enjoy your meal.

1744
01:15:43,340 --> 01:15:45,809
How big do you want them?

1745
01:15:45,809 --> 01:15:48,045
Or we can just scoop it up.

1746
01:15:48,045 --> 01:15:50,614
I don't mind. Anything works for me.

1747
01:15:51,982 --> 01:15:55,285
(Focused)

1748
01:15:55,519 --> 01:15:56,520
Here you go.

1749
01:15:57,855 --> 01:16:00,057
Let's eat.

1750
01:16:00,057 --> 01:16:01,492
Let's eat.

1751
01:16:02,759 --> 01:16:05,262
- The chicken feet smell amazing.
- This looks delicious.

1752
01:16:05,262 --> 01:16:06,964
(Excited)

1753
01:16:08,732 --> 01:16:09,833
Is it good?

1754
01:16:09,833 --> 01:16:11,134
It's so good.

1755
01:16:12,269 --> 01:16:13,470
Yes.

1756
01:16:14,671 --> 01:16:15,839
But it's pretty spicy.

1757
01:16:15,839 --> 01:16:16,974
Can you handle spicy food?

1758
01:16:17,374 --> 01:16:18,709
(Flustered)

1759
01:16:20,611 --> 01:16:21,612
You can't?

1760
01:16:22,946 --> 01:16:24,548
I can handle this much.

1761
01:16:24,548 --> 01:16:25,315
Really?

1762
01:16:25,315 --> 01:16:26,950
(Worried)

1763
01:16:28,051 --> 01:16:29,386
You startled me.

1764
01:16:29,953 --> 01:16:32,656
(His concern slips out.)

1765
01:16:34,758 --> 01:16:35,993
It really is spicy.

1766
01:16:38,695 --> 01:16:40,130
(Stares)

1767
01:16:40,464 --> 01:16:42,032
My gosh.

1768
01:16:42,032 --> 01:16:43,133
(Fluttering)

1769
01:16:43,133 --> 01:16:46,003
Wait. That was so Kang Dong Won.

1770
01:16:46,003 --> 01:16:47,671
That "Temptation of Wolves" angle.

1771
01:16:47,671 --> 01:16:49,173
Was that the umbrella scene?

1772
01:16:49,173 --> 01:16:50,874
That was the umbrella scene.

1773
01:16:53,277 --> 01:16:55,078
When Seon Ho is with Ye Ji,

1774
01:16:55,078 --> 01:16:57,414
he has this special smile.

1775
01:16:57,414 --> 01:16:59,149
He lowers his eyes a little.

1776
01:16:59,149 --> 01:17:01,819
It's the smile he showed
when his heart was pounding.

1777
01:17:02,186 --> 01:17:03,587
One more time?

1778
01:17:03,587 --> 01:17:04,688
Again?

1779
01:17:05,222 --> 01:17:06,957
(Overreacting)

1780
01:17:11,461 --> 01:17:13,530
- Should we order something else?
- No, I'm fine.

1781
01:17:13,530 --> 01:17:15,032
I can have rice balls with it.

1782
01:17:16,834 --> 01:17:19,136
It might be really spicy.

1783
01:17:21,605 --> 01:17:22,973
(Another bite)

1784
01:17:26,877 --> 01:17:32,082
(A sweet spark fills the air.)

1785
01:17:33,550 --> 01:17:35,118
Can I ask you something?

1786
01:17:36,353 --> 01:17:38,989
So...

1787
01:17:38,989 --> 01:17:42,125
age doesn't matter to you at all?

1788
01:17:42,626 --> 01:17:43,594
I...

1789
01:17:44,728 --> 01:17:47,998
prefer someone my age or younger...

1790
01:17:47,998 --> 01:17:50,000
because when I date someone,

1791
01:17:50,000 --> 01:17:52,936
I consider whether we could get married.

1792
01:17:52,936 --> 01:17:54,671
- You seriously consider marriage?
- Yes.

1793
01:17:54,671 --> 01:17:56,907
I want to get married...

1794
01:17:56,907 --> 01:18:00,110
when I'm ready to take responsibility.

1795
01:18:00,377 --> 01:18:02,613
If we felt the same way...

1796
01:18:02,613 --> 01:18:04,181
(Understands)

1797
01:18:04,681 --> 01:18:07,050
When I say,
"I want to marry when I'm ready"...

1798
01:18:07,050 --> 01:18:08,652
You want someone who could wait for you.

1799
01:18:08,652 --> 01:18:09,753
If they can wait, age wouldn't matter?

1800
01:18:09,753 --> 01:18:10,954
Then it wouldn't matter.

1801
01:18:10,954 --> 01:18:12,523
I don't think age matters much.

1802
01:18:13,257 --> 01:18:14,258
But...

1803
01:18:14,258 --> 01:18:15,359
So that was why?

1804
01:18:15,359 --> 01:18:18,462
But practical issues can come up.

1805
01:18:19,096 --> 01:18:21,565
Other than those issues,

1806
01:18:21,565 --> 01:18:24,668
do you have a preferred age range...

1807
01:18:24,668 --> 01:18:26,803
or is any age fine?

1808
01:18:26,803 --> 01:18:28,438
It's not...

1809
01:18:29,273 --> 01:18:30,841
a big deal for me.

1810
01:18:31,775 --> 01:18:33,644
Right. Age isn't everything.

1811
01:18:33,644 --> 01:18:34,611
And you said...

1812
01:18:34,611 --> 01:18:37,214
your brother put you off younger guys.

1813
01:18:38,649 --> 01:18:40,184
So I...

1814
01:18:40,184 --> 01:18:45,255
never considered dating a younger man.

1815
01:18:46,156 --> 01:18:50,127
The person matters more than age.

1816
01:18:50,527 --> 01:18:53,630
I'm changing my mind too.

1817
01:18:53,630 --> 01:18:57,034
I used to only prefer older men.

1818
01:18:57,034 --> 01:19:03,140
But a mature younger man might be okay...

1819
01:19:03,941 --> 01:19:05,008
or someone my age.

1820
01:19:06,610 --> 01:19:07,477
"Because of you?"

1821
01:19:07,477 --> 01:19:09,146
Yes, exactly.

1822
01:19:09,146 --> 01:19:10,380
This is driving me crazy.

1823
01:19:10,380 --> 01:19:11,748
"All because of you."

1824
01:19:11,748 --> 01:19:13,484
She's eating spicy food for him.

1825
01:19:13,484 --> 01:19:15,486
- Right.
- And age no longer matters.

1826
01:19:15,486 --> 01:19:16,620
Today is looking good.

1827
01:19:16,620 --> 01:19:17,621
It's going so well.

1828
01:19:17,621 --> 01:19:19,189
There hasn't been a twist yet.

1829
01:19:19,189 --> 01:19:20,524
Please just let it end like this.

1830
01:19:21,358 --> 01:19:23,527
Don't set this up, then spring a twist.

1831
01:19:23,527 --> 01:19:24,928
If there's a twist, I swear...

1832
01:19:24,928 --> 01:19:26,497
I'm seriously going home.

1833
01:19:29,533 --> 01:19:33,070
(They wonder about each other's age.)

1834
01:19:33,370 --> 01:19:34,638
Should we have another drink?

1835
01:19:37,140 --> 01:19:38,575
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

1836
01:19:39,309 --> 01:19:44,815
(Each drink brings them closer.)

1837
01:19:49,386 --> 01:19:51,421
So at this point,

1838
01:19:51,421 --> 01:19:52,322
Yes?

1839
01:19:52,589 --> 01:19:53,857
this is what we start to consider.

1840
01:19:53,857 --> 01:19:56,727
Will you go all in on one person?

1841
01:19:56,727 --> 01:19:59,563
Or get to know everyone?

1842
01:20:01,598 --> 01:20:02,599
(Ye Ji asks what's on his mind.)

1843
01:20:02,599 --> 01:20:03,867
I was curious about that.

1844
01:20:04,401 --> 01:20:06,003
After yesterday's date...

1845
01:20:06,003 --> 01:20:07,971
I started to feel...

1846
01:20:07,971 --> 01:20:11,408
confused about how Seon Ho felt...

1847
01:20:11,408 --> 01:20:14,645
and unsure of where he stood.

1848
01:20:15,245 --> 01:20:17,281
(After yesterday's date)

1849
01:20:20,117 --> 01:20:21,351
Enjoy your meal.

1850
01:20:21,919 --> 01:20:23,220
Enjoy your meal.

1851
01:20:25,355 --> 01:20:28,725
(The mood subtly shifted afterward.)

1852
01:20:29,660 --> 01:20:30,661
(Grabs)

1853
01:20:31,662 --> 01:20:32,596
That scared me.

1854
01:20:34,097 --> 01:20:36,033
(Glances)

1855
01:20:36,533 --> 01:20:41,104
(Moments when she doubted his feelings)

1856
01:20:41,839 --> 01:20:44,408
I thought we should talk about it,

1857
01:20:44,408 --> 01:20:47,477
so I asked him several questions.

1858
01:20:49,713 --> 01:20:52,182
(Thinks)

1859
01:20:53,447 --> 01:20:55,382
(Nervous)

1860
01:20:58,652 --> 01:21:02,323
First, I'll make the most of our time.

1861
01:21:02,323 --> 01:21:03,724
I'll talk to people...

1862
01:21:03,724 --> 01:21:07,494
because I may find someone I click with.

1863
01:21:15,736 --> 01:21:17,171
Seriously?

1864
01:21:17,171 --> 01:21:18,739
That answer...

1865
01:21:18,739 --> 01:21:21,375
What does that mean?

1866
01:21:21,375 --> 01:21:23,744
"I'll make the most of our time."

1867
01:21:23,744 --> 01:21:26,613
He's saying he'll try to get
to know everyone as much as he can.

1868
01:21:26,613 --> 01:21:27,514
Is that what he means?

1869
01:21:27,514 --> 01:21:29,216
Is that it?

1870
01:21:32,052 --> 01:21:34,154
I really can't read Seon Ho.

1871
01:21:34,555 --> 01:21:35,489
This is hard.

1872
01:21:35,489 --> 01:21:37,658
Seon Ho is so hard to read, right?

1873
01:21:39,693 --> 01:21:44,031
(Seon Ho gives no clear direction.)

1874
01:21:45,099 --> 01:21:50,170
(Ye Ji mulls over his answer.)

1875
01:21:50,738 --> 01:21:52,573
What about you, Ye Ji?

1876
01:21:53,774 --> 01:21:55,576
Can I answer after this drink?

1877
01:21:55,576 --> 01:21:56,644
Sure. Let's have a drink.

1878
01:21:57,211 --> 01:21:58,078
Cheers.

1879
01:22:06,420 --> 01:22:07,821
I...

1880
01:22:09,757 --> 01:22:11,692
(Thinking)

1881
01:22:12,092 --> 01:22:15,496
(He asks Ye Ji the same question.)

1882
01:22:16,930 --> 01:22:17,998
This is hard.

1883
01:22:26,340 --> 01:22:27,808
Honestly,

1884
01:22:30,544 --> 01:22:32,880
before I came here, I was certain...

1885
01:22:33,747 --> 01:22:37,017
I should talk to every single person.

1886
01:22:37,017 --> 01:22:40,220
I thought I'd get to know everyone...

1887
01:22:41,588 --> 01:22:46,293
before making up my mind.

1888
01:22:57,204 --> 01:23:02,676
(The silence between them grows.)

1889
01:23:04,778 --> 01:23:07,781
I'll still talk to the others.

1890
01:23:10,484 --> 01:23:12,086
I don't want any regrets.

1891
01:23:12,086 --> 01:23:13,087
Right.

1892
01:23:19,093 --> 01:23:20,661
The mood was so good.

1893
01:23:20,661 --> 01:23:22,129
It really was.

1894
01:23:22,129 --> 01:23:23,998
- Her face stiffened.
- The mood soured.

1895
01:23:25,299 --> 01:23:26,967
(Sighs)

1896
01:23:27,801 --> 01:23:30,004
Why do they keep missing each other?

1897
01:23:33,540 --> 01:23:34,441
Why aren't you eating?

1898
01:23:38,379 --> 01:23:44,718
(Their time is nearly up.)

1899
01:23:49,790 --> 01:23:54,194
(Their glasses meet in silence.)

1900
01:24:04,738 --> 01:24:06,106
I thought that was mine.

1901
01:24:06,373 --> 01:24:07,408
Was it mine?

1902
01:24:07,408 --> 01:24:08,342
Mine didn't ring.

1903
01:24:09,977 --> 01:24:12,279
(The date lasts for your combined time.)

1904
01:24:12,279 --> 01:24:15,749
(Jung Ye Ji and Kim Seon Ho,
your 100-minute date has ended.)

1905
01:24:15,749 --> 01:24:16,950
What's wrong? Is something up?

1906
01:24:18,152 --> 01:24:21,388
(Ye Ji, 50 minutes / Seon Ho, 50 minutes)

1907
01:24:21,388 --> 01:24:24,458
Now they both know it was 50-50.

1908
01:24:24,458 --> 01:24:26,193
They know they each gave 50 minutes.

1909
01:24:26,193 --> 01:24:27,161
They know.

1910
01:24:27,161 --> 01:24:28,796
(They both gave 50 minutes again.)

1911
01:24:28,796 --> 01:24:30,531
This is tense.

1912
01:24:30,998 --> 01:24:33,968
He can't take his eyes off Ye Ji.

1913
01:24:42,409 --> 01:24:44,912
Just like yesterday,

1914
01:24:45,379 --> 01:24:47,381
the moment I got the same text saying...

1915
01:24:47,381 --> 01:24:49,083
our 100-minute date was over,

1916
01:24:49,083 --> 01:24:52,286
I became sure...

1917
01:24:52,286 --> 01:24:56,023
he must be interested in someone else.

1918
01:24:56,023 --> 01:24:58,492
Neither of us...

1919
01:24:58,492 --> 01:25:01,695
is completely certain yet.

1920
01:25:06,934 --> 01:25:07,901
Shall we clink glasses?

1921
01:25:10,237 --> 01:25:11,105
It's our last drink.

1922
01:25:14,241 --> 01:25:16,810
(Their time stops at 50 minutes.)

1923
01:25:16,810 --> 01:25:20,848
(A crack forms between them.)

1924
01:25:23,684 --> 01:25:24,852
Are we done now?

1925
01:25:25,619 --> 01:25:27,421
Why haven't I gotten a text?

1926
01:25:29,723 --> 01:25:30,858
There it is.

1927
01:25:30,858 --> 01:25:33,127
(The date lasts for your combined time.)

1928
01:25:33,127 --> 01:25:36,864
(Kim Seon Ho and Jung Ye Ji,
your 100-minute date has ended.)

1929
01:25:38,098 --> 01:25:39,333
It's 100 minutes again today.

1930
01:25:40,634 --> 01:25:44,705
We gave each other the same as yesterday.

1931
01:25:45,239 --> 01:25:47,975
Then who was the other person?

1932
01:25:47,975 --> 01:25:51,111
Or were there several other people?

1933
01:25:51,312 --> 01:25:53,247
I had mixed feelings.

1934
01:25:55,082 --> 01:25:57,618
Today felt unusually long.

1935
01:25:58,519 --> 01:26:00,120
What? Wait.

1936
01:26:00,120 --> 01:26:01,288
What did he just say?

1937
01:26:01,288 --> 01:26:02,589
"Unusually long."

1938
01:26:02,589 --> 01:26:03,824
Unusually long?

1939
01:26:03,824 --> 01:26:06,160
Usually, we use that kind of expression...

1940
01:26:06,160 --> 01:26:08,562
in sentences like,
"Today's shoot feels unusually long."

1941
01:26:08,562 --> 01:26:10,097
Exactly.

1942
01:26:10,097 --> 01:26:11,165
Right.

1943
01:26:11,165 --> 01:26:12,833
That's exactly when you'd say it.

1944
01:26:12,833 --> 01:26:13,834
Was he bored?

1945
01:26:13,834 --> 01:26:16,303
"This shoot feels unusually long today."

1946
01:26:16,303 --> 01:26:18,605
(His words could easily be misunderstood.)

1947
01:26:18,605 --> 01:26:20,407
- That's ambiguous.
- Very ambiguous.

1948
01:26:20,407 --> 01:26:23,243
That word is a little ambiguous.

1949
01:26:23,243 --> 01:26:24,945
I feel unusually dizzy today.

1950
01:26:24,945 --> 01:26:26,447
I'm unusually dizzy.

1951
01:26:26,447 --> 01:26:27,748
Today feels unusually...

1952
01:26:27,748 --> 01:26:29,283
I feel unusually frustrated.

1953
01:26:29,283 --> 01:26:31,318
This is unusually confusing.

1954
01:26:31,318 --> 01:26:32,586
It's unusually difficult.

1955
01:26:33,053 --> 01:26:34,555
(Seon Ho's words confuse everyone.)

1956
01:26:34,555 --> 01:26:36,590
- This is hard.
- I'm so confused.

1957
01:26:38,392 --> 01:26:40,494
Today felt unusually long.

1958
01:26:42,396 --> 01:26:43,497
Did you have fun?

1959
01:26:43,497 --> 01:26:44,565
(Nods)

1960
01:26:47,034 --> 01:26:47,935
How about you, Seon Ho?

1961
01:26:47,935 --> 01:26:49,003
I had a great time too.

1962
01:26:52,706 --> 01:26:57,778
(Will their time remain frozen at 50?)

1963
01:27:01,548 --> 01:27:04,652
(Later that night)

1964
01:27:05,519 --> 01:27:08,656
(At the House,)

1965
01:27:09,957 --> 01:27:13,427
(a new relationship begins.)

1966
01:27:13,427 --> 01:27:14,528
It's here.

1967
01:27:14,528 --> 01:27:15,496
Right here?

1968
01:27:15,963 --> 01:27:17,331
Focus, everyone.

1969
01:27:17,331 --> 01:27:18,499
I'll reveal it now.

1970
01:27:20,701 --> 01:27:22,136
Day Three.

1971
01:27:27,441 --> 01:27:31,312
"You may now share all your information."

1972
01:27:32,546 --> 01:27:34,048
You're all so excited.

1973
01:27:34,048 --> 01:27:35,616
"Gather together and talk."

1974
01:27:35,616 --> 01:27:37,718
The moment has finally arrived.

1975
01:27:37,718 --> 01:27:39,753
- Who goes first? I'm losing it.
- I'm dying to know.

1976
01:27:39,753 --> 01:27:40,854
A ballet dancer.

1977
01:27:40,854 --> 01:27:43,324
(Will their ages and jobs sway hearts?)

1978
01:27:43,324 --> 01:27:44,291
No, it's not ballet.

1979
01:27:48,462 --> 01:27:52,833
(Love Against Time)

1980
01:27:52,833 --> 01:27:53,767
I am...

1981
01:27:53,767 --> 01:27:55,035
That's so cool.

1982
01:27:55,035 --> 01:27:56,704
We're the same age.

1983
01:27:56,704 --> 01:27:57,638
A business owner.

1984
01:27:57,638 --> 01:27:58,639
- Wait.
- You're older than me.

1985
01:27:58,639 --> 01:27:59,606
You're older than me.

1986
01:27:59,606 --> 01:28:01,809
Maybe there's more to them than I knew.

1987
01:28:01,809 --> 01:28:04,011
Why does that keep bothering me?

1988
01:28:04,011 --> 01:28:05,112
It's 110 minutes.

1989
01:28:05,112 --> 01:28:06,814
Even if I give 100 minutes now,

1990
01:28:06,814 --> 01:28:08,215
we won't be able to go on a date.

1991
01:28:08,549 --> 01:28:09,950
I have a lot on my mind.

1992
01:28:09,950 --> 01:28:11,051
This can't be happening.

1993
01:28:11,051 --> 01:28:12,519
What a cruel twist of fate.

1994
01:28:12,519 --> 01:28:13,754
The rules changed, so they can't date?

1995
01:28:14,521 --> 01:28:17,124
How did things end up like this?

1996
01:28:17,124 --> 01:28:18,993
Is she not that into me?

1997
01:28:18,993 --> 01:28:21,595
I'll talk to someone I wanted to talk to.

1998
01:28:21,595 --> 01:28:23,530
I did want to talk to you.

1999
01:28:23,530 --> 01:28:25,432
I've really wanted to talk to you.

2000
01:28:25,432 --> 01:28:27,101
(A new connection finds an opening.)

2001
01:28:27,101 --> 01:28:28,636
This is bad.

2002
01:28:28,636 --> 01:28:30,170
Something went wrong.

2003
01:28:30,170 --> 01:28:31,438
That's bad news.

2004
01:28:31,739 --> 01:28:33,741
(The House descends into chaos.
Where will these relationships lead?)

2005
01:28:33,741 --> 01:28:34,842
You scared me.

2006
01:28:34,843 --> 01:28:36,560
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
